WEBVTT

1
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:08,280
[soft, intriguing music playing]

2
00:00:13,840 --> 00:00:16,880
[man] I'm trying to look
like a professional here.

3
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:20,480
-Got it. Nice and neat. Clean.
-[man] Yes, thank you.

4
00:00:21,840 --> 00:00:23,280
[woman] What do you do for work?

5
00:00:24,160 --> 00:00:26,240
[man] Well, I am…

6
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:28,120
Well, before…

7
00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:30,160
How can I say this?

8
00:00:30,680 --> 00:00:33,120
I used to work in finance.

9
00:00:33,720 --> 00:00:36,800
I acquired companies
from the stock market.

10
00:00:36,880 --> 00:00:37,880
[woman] Hmm.

11
00:00:37,960 --> 00:00:41,960
[man] But over the last 30 years,
I've been, uh…

12
00:00:43,480 --> 00:00:44,920
I've been on the run.

13
00:00:45,960 --> 00:00:47,480
-In hiding.
-[woman] In hiding?

14
00:00:47,560 --> 00:00:49,800
[man] Yes, Interpol and everything.

15
00:00:49,880 --> 00:00:52,440
[intriguing music intensifies]

16
00:00:57,400 --> 00:00:59,880
[Karin af Klintberg]
<i>He's been in hiding for 30 years,</i>

17
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:05,520
<i>the man alleged to be behind</i>
<i>one of Sweden's largest financial crimes,</i>

18
00:01:05,600 --> 00:01:07,360
<i>in what came to be known</i>

19
00:01:07,440 --> 00:01:09,280
<i>as the Trustor affair.</i>

20
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:12,360
[reporter 1] <i>The man behind</i>
<i>the suspected fraud</i>

21
00:01:12,440 --> 00:01:14,720
<i>is a 33-year-old from Stockholm.</i>

22
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:17,280
The main perpetrator in the Trustor affair
is Joachim Posener.

23
00:01:17,360 --> 00:01:18,640
[reporter 2] <i>Joachim Posener,</i>

24
00:01:18,720 --> 00:01:21,600
<i>the man suspected</i>
<i>of being the brains behind the operation.</i>

25
00:01:21,680 --> 00:01:24,560
[reporter 3] <i>Joachim Posener is wanted</i>
<i>by Interpol.</i>

26
00:01:25,800 --> 00:01:29,480
[Karin] <i>Rumour has it</i>
<i>that he got away with 100 million,</i>

27
00:01:30,480 --> 00:01:31,840
<i>had plastic surgery</i>

28
00:01:31,920 --> 00:01:35,640
<i>and has been living in hiding</i>
<i>in all corners of the world.</i>

29
00:01:35,720 --> 00:01:36,840
THAT'S WHERE THE FRAUD'S HIDING

30
00:01:36,920 --> 00:01:39,400
[reporter 4] <i>Police have a new lead</i>
<i>regarding his whereabouts.</i>

31
00:01:39,480 --> 00:01:42,240
<i>There was talk about Moscow, Tel Aviv,</i>

32
00:01:42,320 --> 00:01:45,240
<i>Rio de Janeiro, Barbados, Iraq,</i>

33
00:01:45,320 --> 00:01:47,200
<i>and a myriad of other countries.</i>

34
00:01:47,280 --> 00:01:48,800
EXPRESSEN FOUND
SUSPECT'S HOME IN ISRAEL

35
00:01:48,880 --> 00:01:50,920
{\an8}[Karin] <i>A reward was offered</i>
<i>for information</i>

36
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:53,160
{\an8}<i>that could lead to an arrest.</i>

37
00:01:53,680 --> 00:01:56,560
{\an8}<i>The police received tips of all kinds.</i>

38
00:01:56,640 --> 00:01:57,680
THE WANTED JOACHIM POSENER

39
00:01:57,760 --> 00:01:59,760
<i>Some said that he had a ponytail,</i>

40
00:01:59,840 --> 00:02:01,400
<i>very large feet,</i>

41
00:02:01,480 --> 00:02:03,920
<i>spoke with a Scanian accent,</i>

42
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:05,000
<i>drank Pepsi,</i>

43
00:02:05,080 --> 00:02:08,600
<i>and that he was hiding</i>
<i>in the </i>Big Brother <i>house.</i>

44
00:02:09,640 --> 00:02:12,160
<i>But Joachim Posener was never found.</i>

45
00:02:15,440 --> 00:02:18,000
<i>The story goes that in 1997,</i>

46
00:02:18,080 --> 00:02:22,240
<i>he and four other people managed to buy</i>
<i>the investment company Trustor,</i>

47
00:02:23,920 --> 00:02:26,440
<i>using Trustor's own money.</i>

48
00:02:28,720 --> 00:02:32,760
[reporter 1] <i>This is unprecedented in</i>
<i>the history of the Swedish stock exchange.</i>

49
00:02:32,840 --> 00:02:36,000
[reporter 2] <i>Somehow,</i>
<i>hundreds of millions of Trustor's funds</i>

50
00:02:36,080 --> 00:02:39,040
<i>have been traced to bank accounts</i>
<i>all across the world.</i>

51
00:02:39,120 --> 00:02:42,480
[reporter 3] <i>One of the biggest</i>
<i>financial frauds in Swedish history.</i>

52
00:02:44,040 --> 00:02:46,760
[Karin] <i>But how did the whole affair</i>
<i>come to be?</i>

53
00:02:46,840 --> 00:02:48,200
<i>Who did what,</i>

54
00:02:48,680 --> 00:02:51,720
<i>and how did life turn out</i>
<i>for those who were involved?</i>

55
00:02:52,240 --> 00:02:56,320
INSIDE THE TRUSTOR SCANDAL

56
00:02:56,840 --> 00:02:58,960
A FILM BY KARIN AF KLINTBERG

57
00:03:00,280 --> 00:03:03,280
[on radio] <i>♪ Now listen up</i>
<i>Here's the story ♪</i>

58
00:03:03,360 --> 00:03:07,640
<i>♪ About a little guy</i>
<i>that lives in a blue world… ♪</i>

59
00:03:08,160 --> 00:03:11,160
[man] I had no idea what a damn mess
this company takeover would be

60
00:03:11,240 --> 00:03:12,880
when I first got involved.

61
00:03:13,640 --> 00:03:15,960
<i>♪ Inside and outside… ♪</i>

62
00:03:16,040 --> 00:03:18,640
[Karin] <i>This "damn mess"</i>
<i>has been under investigation for years.</i>

63
00:03:18,720 --> 00:03:20,920
<i>Yet what actually happened</i>
<i>still remains unclear,</i>

64
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:23,720
<i>with everyone involved</i>
<i>having their own side of the story.</i>

65
00:03:25,040 --> 00:03:27,600
["Blue (Da Ba Dee)"
by Eiffel 65 continues on radio]

66
00:03:29,360 --> 00:03:30,680
<i>To bring some clarity,</i>

67
00:03:30,760 --> 00:03:34,040
<i>I reached out to those who were involved</i>
<i>in one way or another.</i>

68
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:38,640
<i>One of them</i>
<i>is the consultant Thomas Jisander,</i>

69
00:03:39,160 --> 00:03:41,160
<i>the guy parking his Ferrari.</i>

70
00:03:43,720 --> 00:03:46,520
[Thomas] You might think
I should've known from the start

71
00:03:46,600 --> 00:03:48,960
what was actually going to happen
with this affair.

72
00:03:49,040 --> 00:03:50,000
CONSULTANT, TRUSTOR

73
00:03:50,080 --> 00:03:51,200
But I didn't.

74
00:03:52,600 --> 00:03:54,880
[Karin] <i>I also met the vice president,</i>

75
00:03:54,960 --> 00:03:57,120
<i>who is still affected to this day.</i>

76
00:03:57,640 --> 00:04:01,200
[Richard] Something broke in my brain.
I've barely slept since 1997.

77
00:04:01,280 --> 00:04:02,440
DEPUTY CEO, TRUSTOR, 1997

78
00:04:02,520 --> 00:04:04,960
[Karin]
<i>As well as the investigative reporter.</i>

79
00:04:06,240 --> 00:04:09,480
[Gunnar] I felt in my gut
that something wasn't right.

80
00:04:10,680 --> 00:04:14,520
[Karin] <i>And the police officer</i>
<i>that hunted down Joachim Posener.</i>

81
00:04:14,600 --> 00:04:17,160
[Jochum] It haunts me
that we didn't catch the main suspect

82
00:04:17,240 --> 00:04:19,080
behind the Trustor affair.

83
00:04:19,160 --> 00:04:20,160
Shit.

84
00:04:21,560 --> 00:04:24,200
[Karin] <i>And lastly, the seasoned financier</i>

85
00:04:24,280 --> 00:04:26,520
<i>who tried to clean up the mess.</i>

86
00:04:27,160 --> 00:04:29,720
[Björn] It's one thing
to be tough in business,

87
00:04:29,800 --> 00:04:32,840
but when it comes to criminals,
I have no qualms.

88
00:04:36,640 --> 00:04:38,800
[Karin] <i>And then there's Joachim Posener,</i>

89
00:04:38,880 --> 00:04:42,920
<i>who neither the police nor Interpol</i>
<i>managed to find in those 30 years.</i>

90
00:04:43,440 --> 00:04:45,360
<i>His side of the story has never been told,</i>

91
00:04:45,440 --> 00:04:48,760
{\an8}<i>whether it was worth the price</i>
<i>of leaving his family and children behind</i>

92
00:04:48,840 --> 00:04:50,360
{\an8}<i>to live in hiding.</i>

93
00:04:54,960 --> 00:04:56,960
<i>After an extensive search,</i>

94
00:04:57,040 --> 00:04:59,320
<i>I managed to obtain the email address</i>

95
00:04:59,400 --> 00:05:01,520
<i>of the missing Joachim Posener.</i>

96
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:02,560
SORRY TO NAG…

97
00:05:02,640 --> 00:05:03,960
THIRD TIME LUCKY…

98
00:05:04,040 --> 00:05:06,880
<i>And when I expressed</i>
<i>that I was only looking for the truth…</i>

99
00:05:06,960 --> 00:05:08,800
DIFFICULT TO DETERMINE
WHO'S TELLING THE TRUTH

100
00:05:08,880 --> 00:05:10,280
<i>…he finally replied.</i>

101
00:05:10,360 --> 00:05:11,200
{\an8}INBOX

102
00:05:11,280 --> 00:05:12,280
{\an8}[message alert tone]

103
00:05:12,360 --> 00:05:14,560
[tense music playing]

104
00:05:15,800 --> 00:05:18,120
[Joachim] <i>I got your email and read it.</i>

105
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:20,280
<i>And… okay.</i>

106
00:05:21,480 --> 00:05:23,800
<i>I'll agree to schedule a meeting with you</i>

107
00:05:23,880 --> 00:05:25,760
<i>somewhere in Europe.</i>

108
00:05:28,640 --> 00:05:30,720
[Karin] <i>What are the terms?</i>

109
00:05:31,680 --> 00:05:34,480
[Joachim] <i>I still want</i>
<i>the option to back out.</i>

110
00:05:36,880 --> 00:05:39,640
[Karin] <i>How will I know it's you</i>
<i>when I see you?</i>

111
00:05:40,160 --> 00:05:42,040
[Joachim] <i>You'll recognise this voice.</i>

112
00:05:42,560 --> 00:05:45,280
<i>And even though it's been 30 years,</i>

113
00:05:46,080 --> 00:05:48,440
<i>I don't look that different.</i>

114
00:05:48,520 --> 00:05:50,600
[tense music continues]

115
00:05:50,680 --> 00:05:53,680
BRUSSELS

116
00:05:56,440 --> 00:05:58,720
[Karin] <i>The first meeting</i>
<i>was in a public place,</i>

117
00:05:58,800 --> 00:06:02,240
<i>where Joachim Posener</i>
<i>could watch us from a distance.</i>

118
00:06:03,080 --> 00:06:06,720
<i>The agreement was that we were</i>
<i>only allowed to film him from behind.</i>

119
00:06:09,680 --> 00:06:12,600
<i>No one knows</i>
<i>what he looks like these days.</i>

120
00:06:16,760 --> 00:06:18,360
[music softens]

121
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:33,920
Hello, I'm Joachim.

122
00:06:36,240 --> 00:06:39,840
[Karin] <i>There are very few</i>
<i>official photos of Joachim Posener.</i>

123
00:06:40,360 --> 00:06:44,200
<i>Which makes sense</i>
<i>for someone who doesn't want to be found.</i>

124
00:06:45,840 --> 00:06:49,040
<i>While on the run,</i>
<i>he has given a single TV interview.</i>

125
00:06:49,120 --> 00:06:52,760
<i>But since he was actively wanted</i>
<i>by police at the time,</i>

126
00:06:52,840 --> 00:06:54,520
<i>he didn't want to show his face.</i>

127
00:06:54,600 --> 00:06:57,600
<i>And he lied his way</i>
<i>through the entire interview.</i>

128
00:06:57,680 --> 00:07:01,320
People claim you're the mastermind
behind the Trustor affair. Were you?

129
00:07:01,400 --> 00:07:03,040
[Joachim] No, absolutely not.

130
00:07:03,120 --> 00:07:05,680
I had nothing to do with any of this.

131
00:07:06,200 --> 00:07:09,360
I entered the picture in August.

132
00:07:09,440 --> 00:07:11,160
Before that, I…

133
00:07:11,240 --> 00:07:14,640
[Karin] You've never really
explained what happened.

134
00:07:14,720 --> 00:07:17,520
Why have you decided to come forward now?

135
00:07:17,600 --> 00:07:19,840
[Joachim] We're past
the statute of limitations.

136
00:07:19,920 --> 00:07:22,520
There's no reason to stay silent any more.

137
00:07:23,280 --> 00:07:27,000
[Karin] Will you tell the truth
in our interview? Will you tell the truth?

138
00:07:27,080 --> 00:07:29,120
[Joachim] I definitely won't lie.

139
00:07:29,640 --> 00:07:31,600
-[Karin] About anything?
-[Joachim] No.

140
00:07:31,680 --> 00:07:33,880
But you'll have to ask
the right questions.

141
00:07:34,920 --> 00:07:36,920
[pulsating music playing]

142
00:07:39,320 --> 00:07:40,800
[Karin] <i>The people involved</i>

143
00:07:40,880 --> 00:07:44,200
<i>had their own reasons</i>
<i>for being part of the deal.</i>

144
00:07:48,880 --> 00:07:50,960
[Thomas] To me, it was about making money,

145
00:07:51,040 --> 00:07:53,120
and feeling like I was a success.

146
00:07:53,200 --> 00:07:55,040
Money gives you a kind of freedom,

147
00:07:55,120 --> 00:07:58,240
and it's a confirmation
of whether you're successful or not.

148
00:08:00,520 --> 00:08:01,760
Ever since I was a kid,

149
00:08:01,840 --> 00:08:05,280
I've been fascinated by
big yachts and nice cars.

150
00:08:06,960 --> 00:08:08,120
Excuse me!

151
00:08:08,800 --> 00:08:10,800
Eighty? Eight-zero, right?

152
00:08:11,320 --> 00:08:12,400
What is the model?

153
00:08:12,480 --> 00:08:14,440
I dreamt of becoming very rich,

154
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:17,600
to charter a yacht
after a successful deal,

155
00:08:17,680 --> 00:08:19,960
sit on top of an Acta deck
with a drink in hand

156
00:08:20,040 --> 00:08:22,400
and feel like I did a really good job.

157
00:08:22,920 --> 00:08:24,120
I wanted to make money,

158
00:08:24,200 --> 00:08:26,880
and feel like I deserved
that childhood dream.

159
00:08:30,960 --> 00:08:33,960
[Richard] My dream
was to get into the finance world.

160
00:08:34,040 --> 00:08:35,960
I was obsessed with it.

161
00:08:37,600 --> 00:08:39,640
I used to sell business systems.

162
00:08:39,720 --> 00:08:42,880
Wherever I worked,
I was usually the best salesman.

163
00:08:44,080 --> 00:08:46,600
But what I really wanted
was to be the boss.

164
00:08:47,160 --> 00:08:48,800
Which was a crazy goal,

165
00:08:48,880 --> 00:08:52,000
because it turns out
that I'm not a very good boss.

166
00:08:57,000 --> 00:08:58,960
Back in the day, when you had a yacht,

167
00:08:59,040 --> 00:09:02,920
it had to be at least 100 to 115 feet.

168
00:09:03,440 --> 00:09:06,360
That was the limit
for it to be considered as a yacht.

169
00:09:07,200 --> 00:09:08,560
How long is this one?

170
00:09:09,640 --> 00:09:10,600
Twenty-seven?

171
00:09:10,680 --> 00:09:12,600
These days, standards are a bit higher.

172
00:09:12,680 --> 00:09:17,600
Now, I wouldn't call it a yacht
if it's not at least 165 feet.

173
00:09:17,680 --> 00:09:19,920
Otherwise,
you definitely can't call it a yacht.

174
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:21,640
No one remembers a coward.

175
00:09:27,960 --> 00:09:30,800
[Karin] <i>Joachim Posener</i>
<i>had other motives for the deal.</i>

176
00:09:33,400 --> 00:09:36,160
<i>After our first meeting</i>
<i>with Joachim Posener,</i>

177
00:09:36,240 --> 00:09:39,840
<i>we were allowed to continue meeting</i>
<i>in various locations across Europe.</i>

178
00:09:40,360 --> 00:09:41,400
[Joachim clears throat]

179
00:09:42,200 --> 00:09:43,280
[Joachim] So.

180
00:09:43,800 --> 00:09:45,800
You managed to get me here.

181
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:52,840
[Karin] <i>I was not allowed</i>
<i>to film his face. At least not at first.</i>

182
00:09:54,320 --> 00:09:55,560
<i>He has one rule,</i>

183
00:09:55,640 --> 00:09:57,680
<i>no questions about his family.</i>

184
00:10:00,160 --> 00:10:02,520
<i>It's a rule I'll come to bend eventually.</i>

185
00:10:07,760 --> 00:10:10,920
[Joachim] I still control
every little detail of my life.

186
00:10:12,040 --> 00:10:14,160
It becomes a… habit

187
00:10:14,720 --> 00:10:16,760
when you live life on the run.

188
00:10:21,320 --> 00:10:24,400
{\an8}If you want to avoid being found,
you've got to be bland,

189
00:10:24,480 --> 00:10:26,320
{\an8}uninteresting and invisible.

190
00:10:26,400 --> 00:10:29,440
You've got to disappear
and blend into the crowd.

191
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:34,600
You can't attract anyone's attention.

192
00:10:36,960 --> 00:10:41,440
While on the run from the police,
I lived a bit like a secret agent.

193
00:10:43,720 --> 00:10:47,800
I sacrificed my family
and my life for freedom.

194
00:10:49,040 --> 00:10:50,640
Not for the money.

195
00:10:55,920 --> 00:10:58,440
[Karin] Have you visited Sweden
in the last 30 years?

196
00:10:58,520 --> 00:11:00,000
[Joachim] Not even once.

197
00:11:00,640 --> 00:11:02,400
[Karin] Why didn't you return home?

198
00:11:03,880 --> 00:11:08,560
[Joachim] I couldn't bring myself to serve
a maximum sentence in prison again.

199
00:11:10,760 --> 00:11:14,000
I barely got through
the last sentence I served.

200
00:11:16,120 --> 00:11:18,960
[Karin] <i>"The last sentence"</i>
<i>refers to the prison sentence</i>

201
00:11:19,040 --> 00:11:22,720
<i>that Joachim Posener served</i>
<i>before the Trustor affair.</i>

202
00:11:24,280 --> 00:11:28,600
<i>In the late 1980s,</i>
<i>at the height of the financial boom,</i>

203
00:11:28,680 --> 00:11:34,200
<i>22-year-old Posener had already begun</i>
<i>trading stocks and options,</i>

204
00:11:34,280 --> 00:11:36,560
<i>and selling creative tax solutions.</i>

205
00:11:37,680 --> 00:11:39,600
<i>At first, things went well.</i>

206
00:11:39,680 --> 00:11:42,560
<i>Business was booming</i>
<i>and he was making millions.</i>

207
00:11:43,240 --> 00:11:45,560
[upbeat electronic music playing]

208
00:11:50,760 --> 00:11:53,000
[Joachim] I wanted respect
in the financial world,

209
00:11:53,080 --> 00:11:54,520
even though I didn't belong.

210
00:11:59,520 --> 00:12:02,600
I was young and wanted
to be part of the financial elite.

211
00:12:02,680 --> 00:12:04,040
I wanted everything fast.

212
00:12:04,120 --> 00:12:07,640
I took shortcuts.
I didn't have time for the scenic route.

213
00:12:07,720 --> 00:12:09,920
I hadn't even finished law school.

214
00:12:11,320 --> 00:12:15,040
My greatest fear was
to live this life unnoticed.

215
00:12:15,120 --> 00:12:19,160
And not… leave my mark on the world.

216
00:12:19,240 --> 00:12:20,720
[music fades]

217
00:12:22,520 --> 00:12:24,800
It led to me working extremely hard,

218
00:12:25,320 --> 00:12:27,440
pushing for bigger and better things,

219
00:12:27,520 --> 00:12:30,800
so I could leave a trace
of my existence in this world.

220
00:12:36,880 --> 00:12:40,760
[Karin] <i>Joachim Posener founded</i>
<i>investment company Thul with a colleague.</i>

221
00:12:40,840 --> 00:12:44,680
{\an8}<i>It had offices on fancy streets</i>
<i>in Stockholm and Copenhagen.</i>

222
00:12:46,280 --> 00:12:50,200
{\an8}<i>The only problem was that they</i>
<i>didn't have any money to do business with.</i>

223
00:12:53,240 --> 00:12:56,160
{\an8}[Joachim] In 1991,
during the financial crisis,

224
00:12:56,240 --> 00:12:58,280
{\an8}loans were impossible to get.

225
00:12:58,800 --> 00:13:03,400
But I was able to find a way
to use rigged options.

226
00:13:04,240 --> 00:13:07,360
It doesn't have to exist.
It just needs to look like it does.

227
00:13:07,440 --> 00:13:08,480
[phone dials out]

228
00:13:09,080 --> 00:13:10,440
I had invented a way

229
00:13:10,520 --> 00:13:14,560
to create as many assets as I wanted,
on paper.

230
00:13:14,640 --> 00:13:19,360
That led us to acquiring
four publicly listed companies in Denmark.

231
00:13:21,520 --> 00:13:22,800
But that also meant

232
00:13:22,880 --> 00:13:27,280
that we had acquired them
under not-so-legal circumstances.

233
00:13:30,800 --> 00:13:33,040
I had bought a house

234
00:13:33,560 --> 00:13:34,920
and had just had a daughter.

235
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:36,120
OUR DAUGHTER
JANUARY 13TH

236
00:13:36,200 --> 00:13:38,240
And life was great.

237
00:13:39,200 --> 00:13:41,760
-Then there was a knock at the door.
-[doorbell rings]

238
00:13:41,840 --> 00:13:43,360
And it was the police.

239
00:13:43,880 --> 00:13:45,320
{\an8}[news theme playing]

240
00:13:46,160 --> 00:13:50,280
[reporter] <i>From this house, two Swedes</i>
<i>tried to drain millions from the city.</i>

241
00:13:50,360 --> 00:13:54,000
<i>The masterminds</i>
<i>were sentenced to 6 and 4.5 years</i>

242
00:13:54,080 --> 00:13:55,680
{\an8}<i>for financial fraud.</i>

243
00:13:56,200 --> 00:13:58,600
NORRTÄLJE PRISON

244
00:13:58,680 --> 00:14:02,200
[Karin] <i>Joachim Posener</i>
<i>was permanently expelled from Denmark</i>

245
00:14:02,280 --> 00:14:04,840
<i>and sentenced to six years in prison</i>
<i>in Sweden</i>

246
00:14:04,920 --> 00:14:07,680
<i>for aggravated fraud and tax evasion.</i>

247
00:14:09,040 --> 00:14:12,680
[Joachim] It was such a shock
to receive such a severe sentence

248
00:14:12,760 --> 00:14:15,040
in a high security prison.

249
00:14:16,320 --> 00:14:18,600
I was 29 when I got locked up.

250
00:14:19,120 --> 00:14:20,040
{\an8}It was…

251
00:14:20,120 --> 00:14:22,040
{\an8}THEIR COUP LANDED THEM 500 MILLION

252
00:14:22,120 --> 00:14:24,000
{\an8}…completely devastating.

253
00:14:24,760 --> 00:14:25,760
MARRIED
OWNER OF A VILLA

254
00:14:25,840 --> 00:14:29,880
I lost my house, my wife,
my child, custody.

255
00:14:29,960 --> 00:14:30,880
WEALTH: 1,032,000

256
00:14:30,960 --> 00:14:32,120
Everything was gone.

257
00:14:32,200 --> 00:14:34,080
It was a nightmare.

258
00:14:34,160 --> 00:14:38,960
Going from an upper middle class life
and driving a BMW to work,

259
00:14:39,520 --> 00:14:43,080
to being surrounded by walls
covered in blood and vomit.

260
00:14:46,360 --> 00:14:48,360
The Norrtälje prison.

261
00:14:49,440 --> 00:14:54,280
It was one of Sweden's toughest,
most high-security prisons.

262
00:14:57,720 --> 00:14:58,840
I didn't belong there.

263
00:14:58,920 --> 00:15:02,600
It's for people that are too dangerous
to be around others.

264
00:15:03,120 --> 00:15:05,000
I wasn't in the finance world any more.

265
00:15:06,400 --> 00:15:08,040
You're afraid constantly.

266
00:15:08,120 --> 00:15:10,800
Look at the wrong guy
the wrong way at the wrong time,

267
00:15:10,880 --> 00:15:12,840
and you get beaten up.

268
00:15:12,920 --> 00:15:15,440
They're used to fighting. I'm not.

269
00:15:15,520 --> 00:15:18,000
[alarm buzzing]

270
00:15:18,080 --> 00:15:20,960
The experience
taught me one thing, though.

271
00:15:21,960 --> 00:15:25,280
I never wanted to go through that again.

272
00:15:29,040 --> 00:15:30,840
[Karin] <i>Yet it was in prison,</i>

273
00:15:30,920 --> 00:15:34,200
<i>first in Norrtälje,</i>
<i>then in an open facility,</i>

274
00:15:34,280 --> 00:15:38,320
<i>that Joachim Posener began</i>
<i>planning his next move.</i>

275
00:15:38,920 --> 00:15:41,680
<i>Which would come to be the Trustor Affair.</i>

276
00:15:43,200 --> 00:15:47,040
[Joachim] Within a week,
I was thinking about how to do it again.

277
00:15:47,560 --> 00:15:48,960
But even better.

278
00:15:49,760 --> 00:15:53,080
My mission was to get revenge

279
00:15:53,160 --> 00:15:55,680
and eventually become legit.

280
00:15:55,760 --> 00:15:58,280
[foreboding music playing]

281
00:16:00,160 --> 00:16:01,600
[music stops]

282
00:16:02,600 --> 00:16:05,720
I had made acquiring companies
without funding

283
00:16:05,800 --> 00:16:07,600
my speciality.

284
00:16:08,920 --> 00:16:11,600
And that was the plan this time as well.

285
00:16:12,120 --> 00:16:15,800
I needed to prove to myself
that it could work.

286
00:16:16,440 --> 00:16:19,200
That I could acquire a company
with its own money

287
00:16:19,280 --> 00:16:21,520
without breaking any laws.

288
00:16:24,840 --> 00:16:26,080
[dramatic music playing]

289
00:16:26,160 --> 00:16:29,520
So I started looking
for a publicly listed company

290
00:16:30,080 --> 00:16:33,680
where I could acquire a majority stake
and take control.

291
00:16:34,200 --> 00:16:36,760
It needed to have strong cash reserves

292
00:16:36,840 --> 00:16:40,200
and, ideally, undervalued assets.

293
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:45,920
Whenever I was out on day-release,

294
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:50,640
I would fill bags with financial magazines
and annual reports.

295
00:16:50,720 --> 00:16:54,760
I would walk past the guard
and smuggle them right into the prison.

296
00:16:56,760 --> 00:16:59,080
I had made a list of potential companies.

297
00:17:00,040 --> 00:17:02,160
One of them was Trustor,

298
00:17:02,240 --> 00:17:05,000
but it could've been any company, really.

299
00:17:06,960 --> 00:17:08,640
[music fades]

300
00:17:08,720 --> 00:17:11,640
Since I was in prison,
I needed accomplices.

301
00:17:11,720 --> 00:17:13,880
I couldn't buy listed companies any more.

302
00:17:13,960 --> 00:17:16,960
I was banned from the finance world.
I was burned.

303
00:17:17,880 --> 00:17:19,080
[phone ringing]

304
00:17:19,160 --> 00:17:21,480
That's when my cousin reached out to me.

305
00:17:21,560 --> 00:17:23,720
[phone ringing faintly]

306
00:17:23,800 --> 00:17:24,920
{\an8}[wistful music playing]

307
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:28,320
{\an8}JOACHIM - COUSIN THOMAS

308
00:17:28,920 --> 00:17:31,040
{\an8}[Thomas] Joachim Posener is my cousin.

309
00:17:31,920 --> 00:17:33,680
{\an8}His mother and my mother were sisters.

310
00:17:34,800 --> 00:17:38,400
So we've basically known each other
for our entire lives.

311
00:17:40,840 --> 00:17:44,120
It was around October or November 1996.

312
00:17:44,200 --> 00:17:48,320
Joachim Posener contacted me from prison.
He wanted me to visit him.

313
00:17:51,760 --> 00:17:55,240
[Joachim] Thomas reached out to me
and said he wanted to pay me a visit.

314
00:17:55,320 --> 00:17:56,160
So I said yes.

315
00:17:59,080 --> 00:18:02,960
He started telling me about his Thul deal
and what had happened.

316
00:18:04,200 --> 00:18:05,840
[Joachim] Suddenly, he said,

317
00:18:07,160 --> 00:18:10,560
"If you've got something brewing
that I can be a part of, I want to do it."

318
00:18:10,640 --> 00:18:12,120
"Like you did in Denmark."

319
00:18:14,920 --> 00:18:18,560
[Thomas] Joachim asked me to take part
in the deals he wanted to make.

320
00:18:19,160 --> 00:18:23,400
[Joachim] Thomas nagged his way
into being included, but he knew nothing.

321
00:18:23,480 --> 00:18:24,440
CIVIL ENGINEER

322
00:18:24,520 --> 00:18:27,040
He worked with ISO 9000 certification.

323
00:18:27,120 --> 00:18:28,320
QUALITY ADVISOR - ISO 9000

324
00:18:28,400 --> 00:18:32,480
Yeah, but I mean, I was educated enough
to understand the concept,

325
00:18:33,240 --> 00:18:35,960
even though I hadn't worked
in that field before.

326
00:18:37,200 --> 00:18:40,440
[Joachim] I needed someone
to attend meetings in my place,

327
00:18:40,520 --> 00:18:43,360
and he said he was willing
to do as he was told.

328
00:18:45,280 --> 00:18:47,520
This was my baby, my project.

329
00:18:47,600 --> 00:18:51,160
It was important to me
that I was sole captain of the ship.

330
00:18:53,080 --> 00:18:55,320
But I had failed to anticipate

331
00:18:55,400 --> 00:18:57,880
that Thomas would become
blinded by the money

332
00:18:57,960 --> 00:18:59,920
and start acting stupid.

333
00:19:00,520 --> 00:19:02,200
["Blue (Da Ba Dee)" playing faintly]

334
00:19:02,280 --> 00:19:03,840
Look who's here! Welcome!

335
00:19:03,920 --> 00:19:06,600
This is my home. This is the living room.

336
00:19:07,480 --> 00:19:12,560
And… there's my little conference table
and the dining room.

337
00:19:12,640 --> 00:19:14,680
A big American-style sofa.

338
00:19:14,760 --> 00:19:16,160
And here…

339
00:19:16,720 --> 00:19:18,280
is where I keep my bubbly.

340
00:19:20,560 --> 00:19:23,000
Which I drink whenever I'm thirsty.

341
00:19:23,960 --> 00:19:25,480
And that happens quite often.

342
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:28,280
So yeah, it's a refrigerator, actually.

343
00:19:28,360 --> 00:19:31,120
And then, uh,
I have a lovely view over Monaco.

344
00:19:33,520 --> 00:19:35,440
Think I'm gonna pour myself a drink.

345
00:19:36,280 --> 00:19:37,840
God, it's so bright.

346
00:19:43,240 --> 00:19:44,680
That tastes good.

347
00:19:45,680 --> 00:19:48,680
Here's a mini barbecue
and a small fridge. A caviar fridge.

348
00:19:49,200 --> 00:19:50,440
Right, let's move on.

349
00:19:50,520 --> 00:19:54,160
I've got a few coffee machines,
ice makers and stuff.

350
00:19:54,680 --> 00:19:57,480
And this is the bedroom. It's Versace.

351
00:19:57,560 --> 00:19:59,520
I only want the best,
so that's what I get.

352
00:20:00,400 --> 00:20:03,400
2,100 square feet in a prime location.

353
00:20:03,480 --> 00:20:04,840
Yup. Feels quite good.

354
00:20:05,360 --> 00:20:06,760
Gets the job done.

355
00:20:08,720 --> 00:20:11,280
[intriguing music playing]

356
00:20:11,360 --> 00:20:15,000
[Karin] <i>The cousins grew up</i>
<i>in good middle class neighbourhoods.</i>

357
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:17,920
{\an8}<i>Jisander in Askim in Gothenburg…</i>

358
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:19,080
{\an8}IN FRONT OF THE VILLA

359
00:20:19,160 --> 00:20:21,680
{\an8}<i>…and Posener in Lidingö in Stockholm.</i>

360
00:20:22,200 --> 00:20:23,560
{\an8}JOACHIM IS GOING ICE-SKATING

361
00:20:23,640 --> 00:20:25,320
[Joachim] I wasn't a cool kid.

362
00:20:26,480 --> 00:20:30,040
But I had a strong feeling
that nothing was impossible.

363
00:20:32,200 --> 00:20:35,240
[Karin] When was the first time
you took an unlawful loan?

364
00:20:35,840 --> 00:20:39,080
[Joachim] I was part of a financial club
in college.

365
00:20:39,600 --> 00:20:42,320
I think I was 17 or 18.

366
00:20:42,400 --> 00:20:45,800
And I needed to pay for something,
and they had cash.

367
00:20:45,880 --> 00:20:47,000
So I took it.

368
00:20:47,080 --> 00:20:48,760
I intended to pay it back,

369
00:20:48,840 --> 00:20:51,560
but they found out it was missing
before I could.

370
00:20:52,080 --> 00:20:55,640
It must've been…
I don't remember. 10,000 krona.

371
00:20:57,720 --> 00:21:00,800
[Karin] Do you think
that was a sign of things to come?

372
00:21:01,760 --> 00:21:05,880
[Joachim] I think it has more to do
with how I look on laws and regulations.

373
00:21:05,960 --> 00:21:08,320
I try to follow the laws as best I can,

374
00:21:08,400 --> 00:21:11,720
but when they don't suit me,
I see them as guidelines.

375
00:21:16,800 --> 00:21:19,600
[Karin] <i>When he is temporarily</i>
<i>allowed to leave prison,</i>

376
00:21:19,680 --> 00:21:21,200
<i>Posener takes liberties.</i>

377
00:21:21,280 --> 00:21:23,440
<i>He attends business meetings</i>
<i>across Europe,</i>

378
00:21:23,520 --> 00:21:26,160
<i>even though he isn't allowed</i>
<i>to leave the country.</i>

379
00:21:28,400 --> 00:21:31,680
<i>After four years,</i>
<i>he is released, but on parole.</i>

380
00:21:33,480 --> 00:21:35,400
[Thomas] He got out in February 1997.

381
00:21:35,480 --> 00:21:36,320
RELEASED!

382
00:21:36,400 --> 00:21:38,760
He needed a place to stay.

383
00:21:39,360 --> 00:21:42,200
I had an apartment I wasn't using,
so I let him use it.

384
00:21:44,040 --> 00:21:46,400
[Karin] <i>Posener is under supervision</i>

385
00:21:46,480 --> 00:21:48,680
<i>and banned from commercial activities.</i>

386
00:21:49,200 --> 00:21:51,520
<i>But that doesn't matter</i>
<i>if you're invisible.</i>

387
00:21:52,720 --> 00:21:55,960
[Joachim] After a while,
I realised we needed more accomplices

388
00:21:56,040 --> 00:21:59,560
to help us get there
and to open some doors.

389
00:22:00,080 --> 00:22:04,040
{\an8}And that's when Thomas suggested
his friend Peter Mattsson.

390
00:22:04,120 --> 00:22:05,960
{\an8}[tense music playing]

391
00:22:06,040 --> 00:22:07,920
{\an8}[indistinct chatter and laughter]

392
00:22:08,520 --> 00:22:12,240
Peter Mattsson
was from a wealthy family in Gothenburg.

393
00:22:14,240 --> 00:22:18,960
To me, Peter Mattsson's biggest asset
was that he knew a British Lord.

394
00:22:19,040 --> 00:22:21,520
A Lord who fit my plan perfectly.

395
00:22:22,040 --> 00:22:25,640
{\an8}[man] Peter Mattsson came to me
with this proposition and said,

396
00:22:25,720 --> 00:22:29,080
{\an8}"There are these people
who want you to front them

397
00:22:29,160 --> 00:22:31,080
buying Trustor."

398
00:22:34,600 --> 00:22:36,720
[Karin] <i>Lord Moyne is from the successful</i>

399
00:22:36,800 --> 00:22:38,760
<i>brewery family Guinness.</i>

400
00:22:39,320 --> 00:22:41,360
<i>He is indeed a British Lord.</i>

401
00:22:41,440 --> 00:22:44,400
<i>But for a Lord, he is a bit strange.</i>

402
00:22:45,160 --> 00:22:47,240
<i>He wears worn out loafers</i>

403
00:22:47,840 --> 00:22:49,440
<i>and Rastafari bracelets.</i>

404
00:22:50,480 --> 00:22:52,200
<i>He practices yoga.</i>

405
00:22:52,280 --> 00:22:54,920
<i>He lives with his wife, Sue,</i>
<i>during the week,</i>

406
00:22:55,000 --> 00:22:58,120
<i>and with his mistress, Shoe, on weekends.</i>

407
00:22:58,880 --> 00:23:01,600
<i>Business was not his cup of tea.</i>

408
00:23:02,880 --> 00:23:04,760
<i>But the Lord needed money.</i>

409
00:23:05,280 --> 00:23:06,760
<i>And he would get it,</i>

410
00:23:06,840 --> 00:23:09,920
<i>so long as he fronted</i>
<i>the acquisition of Trustor.</i>

411
00:23:11,640 --> 00:23:14,440
[Joachim] He was my hired figurehead.

412
00:23:16,520 --> 00:23:18,680
With a British Lord on board,

413
00:23:18,760 --> 00:23:22,920
I knew that every single door
was now open for us.

414
00:23:23,880 --> 00:23:27,360
The world of finance
was eating out of his hand.

415
00:23:29,040 --> 00:23:32,120
[Karin] <i>No one suspected</i>
<i>anything was amiss.</i>

416
00:23:32,200 --> 00:23:34,360
<i>The Lord was presented</i>
<i>as a business genius</i>

417
00:23:34,440 --> 00:23:36,000
<i>who wanted to invest in the Nordics.</i>

418
00:23:36,080 --> 00:23:37,760
<i>As proof of his wealth,</i>

419
00:23:37,840 --> 00:23:40,240
<i>the trio showcased a British magazine</i>

420
00:23:40,320 --> 00:23:44,200
<i>which claimed he was</i>
<i>one of England's 500 richest people.</i>

421
00:23:45,360 --> 00:23:49,120
<i>But they never told anyone</i>
<i>that this was a factual error.</i>

422
00:23:55,000 --> 00:23:58,520
[Joachim] I had my frontman
and I had my two assistants,

423
00:23:58,600 --> 00:24:02,080
{\an8}but a publicly listed company needs a CEO.

424
00:24:03,120 --> 00:24:06,160
{\an8}I didn't really care who,
as long as he was cooperative

425
00:24:06,760 --> 00:24:09,560
and knew that I'd be the one
calling the shots.

426
00:24:09,640 --> 00:24:13,920
And Peter said, "You know what?
I know a guy, he's great."

427
00:24:14,640 --> 00:24:16,320
{\an8}Lindsay Smallbone.

428
00:24:16,400 --> 00:24:18,400
{\an8}[intriguing music playing]

429
00:24:19,080 --> 00:24:22,640
[Karin] <i>Lindsay Smallbone</i>
<i>was from New Zealand but lived in London.</i>

430
00:24:22,720 --> 00:24:26,000
<i>He moved in high society circles</i>
<i>alongside Lord Moyne.</i>

431
00:24:27,200 --> 00:24:30,680
<i>He lived an extravagant life</i>
<i>and had accumulated debts,</i>

432
00:24:30,760 --> 00:24:33,760
<i>so the Trustor job offer</i>
<i>came at an opportune time.</i>

433
00:24:35,520 --> 00:24:38,440
<i>And so Team Moyne was ready.</i>

434
00:24:41,240 --> 00:24:44,080
[Joachim] From prison,
the best people I could recruit

435
00:24:44,160 --> 00:24:47,520
were the party boys,
Jisander and Mattsson.

436
00:24:49,720 --> 00:24:50,800
And those…

437
00:24:51,400 --> 00:24:53,520
[sighs] …well, amateurs,

438
00:24:53,600 --> 00:24:55,520
Lord Moyne and Lindsay Smallbone.

439
00:24:56,040 --> 00:24:57,800
It was kind of an amateur move,

440
00:24:57,880 --> 00:25:01,200
but back then, you couldn't
look people up online, on Google.

441
00:25:01,280 --> 00:25:02,600
That didn't exist.

442
00:25:04,480 --> 00:25:05,520
I chose wrong,

443
00:25:06,680 --> 00:25:08,080
it turned out.

444
00:25:10,840 --> 00:25:13,840
I should've chosen anyone
but Lindsay Smallbone.

445
00:25:15,080 --> 00:25:17,280
He was the one who ruined everything.

446
00:25:19,720 --> 00:25:21,440
To me, they were just frontmen.

447
00:25:21,960 --> 00:25:25,680
And to afford them,
and the other costs from the acquisition,

448
00:25:25,760 --> 00:25:28,480
I borrowed money from the underworld.

449
00:25:30,120 --> 00:25:33,920
Hardened criminals
that I'd met in prison in Norrtälje.

450
00:25:34,480 --> 00:25:37,440
Because I couldn't borrow
from anyone else.

451
00:25:37,520 --> 00:25:39,600
[sinister music playing]

452
00:25:39,680 --> 00:25:43,120
I offered them a return of 20 million

453
00:25:43,200 --> 00:25:45,560
if they'd lend me one million.

454
00:25:47,560 --> 00:25:50,360
And you don't play games
with these people.

455
00:25:51,880 --> 00:25:53,280
They would kill you.

456
00:25:54,200 --> 00:25:57,480
So failure was not an option.

457
00:26:03,360 --> 00:26:06,080
[Karin] <i>In the spring of 1997,</i>

458
00:26:06,160 --> 00:26:08,520
{\an8}<i>another person was brought onto the team.</i>

459
00:26:08,600 --> 00:26:11,120
{\an8}<i>In quite an informal interview process,</i>

460
00:26:11,200 --> 00:26:14,240
{\an8}<i>Richard Djursén was recruited at the gym.</i>

461
00:26:15,720 --> 00:26:18,880
{\an8}I met Thomas Jisander
in front of a mirror at the gym.

462
00:26:18,960 --> 00:26:21,200
[rousing synth pop playing]

463
00:26:25,800 --> 00:26:27,560
[Thomas] I was doing bicep curls.

464
00:26:27,640 --> 00:26:30,480
[Richard] We were there
talking to ourselves in the mirror.

465
00:26:30,560 --> 00:26:33,400
[Thomas] Another dude
was talking to himself in the mirror.

466
00:26:33,480 --> 00:26:36,920
He was looking at his biceps.
"Look at these guns," he said.

467
00:26:39,600 --> 00:26:43,280
[Richard] After a while,
we decided to talk to each other instead.

468
00:26:45,480 --> 00:26:47,240
And we became friends.

469
00:26:52,960 --> 00:26:55,160
Thomas said he had something in the works

470
00:26:55,680 --> 00:26:57,920
and that I could be a part of it.

471
00:26:58,840 --> 00:27:01,040
I was dying to change jobs.

472
00:27:01,120 --> 00:27:03,240
I wanted to get into finance.

473
00:27:03,320 --> 00:27:06,240
And this allowed me
to make that career move.

474
00:27:06,320 --> 00:27:07,480
[music ends]

475
00:27:08,440 --> 00:27:11,800
Since I was a kid,
I dreamed about buying a house.

476
00:27:11,880 --> 00:27:13,040
My own house.

477
00:27:13,560 --> 00:27:16,880
So what's always driven me
is the will to build a house.

478
00:27:16,960 --> 00:27:19,320
I didn't want money,
I just wanted a house.

479
00:27:20,200 --> 00:27:22,520
And I've worked very hard to achieve that.

480
00:27:22,600 --> 00:27:26,440
You can tell I have an inferiority complex
by the size of my house.

481
00:27:29,720 --> 00:27:32,880
I was raised by a single mother
who cleaned hotel rooms.

482
00:27:32,960 --> 00:27:35,240
She worked hard,
but we never had any money.

483
00:27:35,760 --> 00:27:39,040
So when I met other kids
who got bikes and mopeds and…

484
00:27:39,120 --> 00:27:41,360
You know, I never got anything.

485
00:27:41,440 --> 00:27:45,840
It wasn't because my mother was stingy,
she simply couldn't afford it.

486
00:27:45,920 --> 00:27:49,640
And later on,
I was placed in a foster home.

487
00:27:51,480 --> 00:27:54,080
The napkins
won't match perfectly this time,

488
00:27:54,160 --> 00:27:56,040
but it'll do the job.

489
00:27:59,320 --> 00:28:02,240
At Trustor,
my role was to serve as vice president…

490
00:28:02,320 --> 00:28:03,320
CERTIFICATE
DEPUTY CEO

491
00:28:03,400 --> 00:28:04,840
…and head of office

492
00:28:05,720 --> 00:28:07,760
at the office in Stockholm.

493
00:28:09,800 --> 00:28:12,880
In the spring,
I knew nothing of Joachim Posener.

494
00:28:13,720 --> 00:28:16,760
I later found out
he had been involved in financial fraud,

495
00:28:16,840 --> 00:28:19,160
but I wasn't aware of that back then.

496
00:28:19,960 --> 00:28:21,120
[Joachim clears throat]

497
00:28:21,840 --> 00:28:24,600
All of my frontmen knew everything.

498
00:28:29,600 --> 00:28:32,200
Who I was, that I was Joachim Posener.

499
00:28:32,280 --> 00:28:35,000
They knew that I was the one
buying Trustor.

500
00:28:38,160 --> 00:28:40,680
If you think everyone in the group
knew everything…

501
00:28:41,200 --> 00:28:42,960
You're wrong. We didn't.

502
00:28:43,040 --> 00:28:47,200
[Joachim] Djursén and Jisander
both knew there was no money.

503
00:28:47,280 --> 00:28:48,560
At the time, none of us knew

504
00:28:48,640 --> 00:28:51,400
the company was being acquired
using its own money.

505
00:28:52,200 --> 00:28:55,960
{\an8}[Joachim] They knew I bought the company
using its own money.

506
00:28:58,000 --> 00:29:01,200
{\an8}Once again, everyone knew everything.

507
00:29:02,960 --> 00:29:05,160
{\an8}But it all leads back to me.

508
00:29:07,600 --> 00:29:09,320
Because I'm the one who did it.

509
00:29:13,640 --> 00:29:16,400
[Karin] You now want to show your face.

510
00:29:17,320 --> 00:29:19,200
Can you tell us why now?

511
00:29:21,200 --> 00:29:23,920
I realised it's time to be fully honest.

512
00:29:24,440 --> 00:29:25,760
I own what I've done.

513
00:29:27,120 --> 00:29:28,360
I'll show my face now,

514
00:29:28,440 --> 00:29:30,960
but then I'll disappear again.

515
00:29:31,480 --> 00:29:33,480
[suspenseful music playing]

516
00:30:06,240 --> 00:30:08,360
The plan was perfect.

517
00:30:09,640 --> 00:30:12,440
But some things
are just out of your control.

518
00:30:15,080 --> 00:30:17,080
[tense, pulsating music playing]

519
00:30:18,480 --> 00:30:20,880
[Karin] <i>Joachim Posener</i>
<i>stays in the background</i>

520
00:30:20,960 --> 00:30:25,320
<i>as the negotiations with Trustor begin</i>
<i>in the spring of 1997.</i>

521
00:30:28,040 --> 00:30:30,680
I got very good
at managing my assistants remotely,

522
00:30:30,760 --> 00:30:31,920
like running a

523
00:30:32,640 --> 00:30:34,760
little puppet show.

524
00:30:36,120 --> 00:30:39,320
I called Thomas and told him what to say,

525
00:30:40,200 --> 00:30:41,720
and he did great.

526
00:30:42,600 --> 00:30:45,760
He was obedient,
a quick learner, and easy to control.

527
00:30:46,280 --> 00:30:48,840
Thomas's job was to be my assistant.

528
00:30:50,560 --> 00:30:52,200
[Thomas] I wasn't just a mouthpiece.

529
00:30:52,800 --> 00:30:55,840
Lots of small decisions
had to be made on the fly.

530
00:30:56,560 --> 00:30:58,640
[Joachim] I got calls daily
from my gangster friends,

531
00:30:58,720 --> 00:31:01,040
demanding I pay them back immediately,

532
00:31:01,120 --> 00:31:04,280
so I needed to close this deal
as soon as possible.

533
00:31:05,480 --> 00:31:06,880
[enigmatic music playing]

534
00:31:06,960 --> 00:31:08,680
[Karin] <i>But how will Posener</i>

535
00:31:08,760 --> 00:31:13,480
<i>convince Trustor's founder and owner,</i>
<i>Per-Olov Norberg, to sell?</i>

536
00:31:14,800 --> 00:31:16,640
<i>Trustor was an investment firm</i>

537
00:31:16,720 --> 00:31:18,680
{\an8}<i>that didn't produce anything itself,</i>

538
00:31:18,760 --> 00:31:20,720
{\an8}<i>but bought and sold other companies.</i>

539
00:31:21,400 --> 00:31:22,440
{\an8}<i>And at the time,</i>

540
00:31:22,520 --> 00:31:25,560
{\an8}<i>its portfolio held</i>
<i>several valuable assets.</i>

541
00:31:25,640 --> 00:31:28,400
{\an8}COMPANY
1 - 2 - 3 - 4 - 5

542
00:31:28,480 --> 00:31:31,760
{\an8}[Joachim] The owner, Norberg,
had undervalued these assets.

543
00:31:32,520 --> 00:31:35,840
{\an8}He was willing to sell, on one condition.

544
00:31:35,920 --> 00:31:38,800
{\an8}That he could buy back some assets later

545
00:31:38,880 --> 00:31:41,320
{\an8}at a more favourable price.

546
00:31:45,000 --> 00:31:47,200
Of course,
I would give him what he wanted,

547
00:31:48,760 --> 00:31:50,920
if he gave me what I wanted.

548
00:31:54,080 --> 00:31:56,880
He would have the option
to buy back Trustor's assets.

549
00:31:56,960 --> 00:32:00,320
And with that sale,
I would bring cash into the company.

550
00:32:00,840 --> 00:32:02,520
I didn't have any money.

551
00:32:03,800 --> 00:32:05,800
[wistful music playing]

552
00:32:06,360 --> 00:32:10,560
[Karin] <i>Joachim Posener</i>
<i>only needed to buy 17% of the shares</i>

553
00:32:10,640 --> 00:32:12,920
<i>to take control of Trustor.</i>

554
00:32:13,000 --> 00:32:15,360
<i>These were high-voting A shares,</i>

555
00:32:15,440 --> 00:32:19,280
<i>and by acquiring them,</i>
<i>he would gain a majority in the company</i>

556
00:32:19,360 --> 00:32:22,200
<i>and have access to its cash reserves.</i>

557
00:32:24,520 --> 00:32:26,760
I needed a short-term loan.

558
00:32:27,360 --> 00:32:31,720
The price tag for the Trustor shares
was a quarter of a billion krona.

559
00:32:31,800 --> 00:32:34,960
If I could borrow that amount
for a single day,

560
00:32:35,040 --> 00:32:36,880
I could pay for the shares,

561
00:32:37,400 --> 00:32:39,600
take control of the cash reserves,

562
00:32:39,680 --> 00:32:42,800
and then immediately pay back the loan.

563
00:32:44,200 --> 00:32:47,600
It was simple. 24 hours was all I needed.

564
00:32:49,040 --> 00:32:51,400
[Thomas] Joachim asked me
to find a financier.

565
00:32:51,960 --> 00:32:55,840
I managed to bring in a billionaire
who was willing to provide a loan.

566
00:32:56,360 --> 00:32:59,000
That's essentially bridge financing,

567
00:32:59,600 --> 00:33:01,160
and it's perfectly legal.

568
00:33:01,760 --> 00:33:04,960
[Joachim] The loan was secured,
but a legal obstacle emerged.

569
00:33:05,040 --> 00:33:08,360
A majority shareholder or board member
of a listed company

570
00:33:08,440 --> 00:33:10,840
cannot purchase the company's own assets.

571
00:33:10,920 --> 00:33:11,800
I resolved this

572
00:33:11,880 --> 00:33:14,880
by getting Norberg to resign
before the deal.

573
00:33:15,640 --> 00:33:17,880
That gave me an unexpected advantage.

574
00:33:18,400 --> 00:33:21,600
I suddenly had a five-day extension
on the payment,

575
00:33:21,680 --> 00:33:24,400
and didn't need the loan
from Thomas's billionaire.

576
00:33:28,040 --> 00:33:30,960
[Thomas] After all this,
Joachim told me the financier I'd found

577
00:33:31,040 --> 00:33:32,280
was no longer needed.

578
00:33:32,800 --> 00:33:34,760
He had come up with another solution.

579
00:33:38,600 --> 00:33:44,360
[Karin] <i>Posener had put together</i>
<i>a massive "buy now, pay later" deal.</i>

580
00:33:44,880 --> 00:33:47,200
<i>But that created two major problems.</i>

581
00:33:47,280 --> 00:33:52,120
<i>The purchase price of 241 million</i>
<i>left a hole in Trustor's cash flow</i>

582
00:33:52,200 --> 00:33:54,640
<i>that sooner or later</i>
<i>would need to be covered.</i>

583
00:33:55,160 --> 00:33:58,800
<i>And buying a company using its own money</i>

584
00:33:58,880 --> 00:34:00,200
<i>is illegal.</i>

585
00:34:04,600 --> 00:34:09,040
Everything was ready. All that was missing
was Lord Moyne's signature.

586
00:34:09,920 --> 00:34:13,200
That's when I realised
I had a big decision to make.

587
00:34:15,640 --> 00:34:20,160
I wasn't able to find a way
to make the acquisition legal.

588
00:34:20,720 --> 00:34:22,760
I knew that, but did it anyway.

589
00:34:23,840 --> 00:34:25,120
It was a gamble.

590
00:34:26,840 --> 00:34:30,080
[Karin] This is where we differ.
I wouldn't have made that choice.

591
00:34:31,120 --> 00:34:32,680
I thought it would work.

592
00:34:35,960 --> 00:34:37,680
[tense, pulsating music playing]

593
00:34:37,760 --> 00:34:41,080
JUNE 12, 1997

594
00:34:41,160 --> 00:34:43,160
[helicopter whirring]

595
00:34:47,720 --> 00:34:51,040
[Joachim] I wasn't in the room
when the deal with Norberg was signed.

596
00:34:51,840 --> 00:34:56,360
But I had meticulously planned out
the meeting… beforehand.

597
00:34:56,880 --> 00:34:59,480
Everyone knew what their job was,
and did it.

598
00:35:00,960 --> 00:35:04,320
[Thomas] The deal was signed
at Erik Penser Corporate Finance.

599
00:35:04,400 --> 00:35:07,440
{\an8}They had gathered
Per-Olov Norberg as the seller,

600
00:35:07,520 --> 00:35:08,840
Lord Moyne as the buyer,

601
00:35:08,920 --> 00:35:10,280
I was there as a consultant,

602
00:35:10,880 --> 00:35:12,240
Peter Mattsson was there,

603
00:35:12,320 --> 00:35:15,560
and Erik Penser himself,
along with three of his staff members.

604
00:35:17,560 --> 00:35:18,920
[Joachim] I sat in my room

605
00:35:19,000 --> 00:35:21,560
waiting for a call
to say that it was done.

606
00:35:23,080 --> 00:35:27,800
I didn't have the slightest suspicion
there was anything wrong with the deal.

607
00:35:28,880 --> 00:35:30,920
It was sanctioned at every level.

608
00:35:32,560 --> 00:35:34,200
And finally, the call came.

609
00:35:34,280 --> 00:35:35,440
[phone rings]

610
00:35:35,520 --> 00:35:36,840
It was Thomas.

611
00:35:37,440 --> 00:35:38,680
"It's done, Jocke!"

612
00:35:38,760 --> 00:35:40,000
[wistful music playing]

613
00:35:40,080 --> 00:35:42,120
[Thomas] When the agreement was signed,

614
00:35:42,200 --> 00:35:44,520
it was a fantastic moment for everyone.

615
00:35:45,040 --> 00:35:46,600
It was a massive accomplishment.

616
00:35:47,120 --> 00:35:48,760
We actually pulled it off.

617
00:35:49,280 --> 00:35:50,240
Done deal.

618
00:35:51,280 --> 00:35:52,360
Yes, well…

619
00:35:53,200 --> 00:35:54,480
Champagne o'clock!

620
00:35:54,560 --> 00:35:57,760
[Joachim] Finally, after four years,
the deal had come together.

621
00:35:57,840 --> 00:36:00,960
And then it was just, "Wow, I'm back."

622
00:36:01,040 --> 00:36:02,040
[cork pops]

623
00:36:02,640 --> 00:36:03,640
There we go.

624
00:36:06,520 --> 00:36:09,400
[pulsating electronic music playing]

625
00:36:16,120 --> 00:36:20,200
[Karin] <i>Team Moyne had full access</i>
<i>to Trustor's cash reserves.</i>

626
00:36:20,880 --> 00:36:22,600
<i>But they weren't finished yet.</i>

627
00:36:23,120 --> 00:36:26,280
<i>They still needed to arrange</i>
<i>the payments for the loan.</i>

628
00:36:26,360 --> 00:36:28,320
<i>And they had five days to do it.</i>

629
00:36:29,520 --> 00:36:32,720
<i>Posener sent the group to a bank in London</i>

630
00:36:32,800 --> 00:36:34,840
<i>to open several new accounts.</i>

631
00:36:38,480 --> 00:36:39,880
This is the place.

632
00:36:41,680 --> 00:36:42,680
[camera clicks]

633
00:36:44,000 --> 00:36:46,480
The same day they walked in there,

634
00:36:46,560 --> 00:36:50,680
Richard Djursén
walked into a bank in Stockholm.

635
00:36:51,280 --> 00:36:52,920
[Richard] I was 35 years old

636
00:36:53,000 --> 00:36:56,720
and got to be part
of a 620 million transaction.

637
00:36:56,800 --> 00:37:00,800
I thought I'd finally made it
in the finance industry.

638
00:37:01,320 --> 00:37:02,840
That's where I wanted to be.

639
00:37:04,720 --> 00:37:08,040
[Karin] <i>Djursén transferred</i>
<i>Trustor's money from Sweden</i>

640
00:37:08,120 --> 00:37:10,600
<i>to Trustor's newly opened account</i>
<i>in England.</i>

641
00:37:11,200 --> 00:37:14,320
<i>There, the money passed</i>
<i>through Thomas Jisander's account,</i>

642
00:37:14,400 --> 00:37:16,480
<i>before being sent on to Lord Moyne,</i>

643
00:37:16,560 --> 00:37:18,360
<i>who paid the former owner.</i>

644
00:37:19,640 --> 00:37:23,000
<i>So it looked as though the payment</i>
<i>was coming from the Lord.</i>

645
00:37:23,960 --> 00:37:25,640
[Joachim] What made it illegal

646
00:37:25,720 --> 00:37:29,560
was when I told Thomas

647
00:37:29,640 --> 00:37:32,200
to send money from Trustor's account

648
00:37:32,280 --> 00:37:33,920
to his own account,

649
00:37:34,000 --> 00:37:35,920
and then on to Lord Moyne,

650
00:37:36,000 --> 00:37:40,520
and then that Norberg was paid
with the company's own money.

651
00:37:41,280 --> 00:37:42,480
[Thomas clears throat]

652
00:37:43,520 --> 00:37:45,520
I wasn't that involved in that.

653
00:37:45,600 --> 00:37:48,480
Joachim claimed
to have financing in place.

654
00:37:49,480 --> 00:37:53,040
I was instructed to open an agent account
at Barclays Bank,

655
00:37:53,120 --> 00:37:56,600
in order to receive money
from the financier in question.

656
00:37:57,320 --> 00:37:59,200
Who that was, I didn't know.

657
00:37:59,960 --> 00:38:02,200
[Karin] But you knew there was no money?

658
00:38:04,040 --> 00:38:06,920
-How would have I known?
-[Karin] You must've talked.

659
00:38:08,320 --> 00:38:10,360
The money came from the financier.

660
00:38:10,440 --> 00:38:11,560
That was how I saw it.

661
00:38:11,640 --> 00:38:15,080
I forwarded it to Lord Moyne,
who paid Per-Olov Norberg.

662
00:38:15,160 --> 00:38:17,000
Very straightforward deal.

663
00:38:17,080 --> 00:38:18,240
End of story.

664
00:38:19,280 --> 00:38:22,160
The deal was done. Trustor was mine.

665
00:38:22,840 --> 00:38:25,440
[enigmatic string music playing]

666
00:38:28,480 --> 00:38:32,640
I was sitting on a plane,
and I was looking around.

667
00:38:33,160 --> 00:38:36,120
Everything was good in my life.
I owned Trustor.

668
00:38:37,000 --> 00:38:39,920
And I thought, "Nobody knows it…

669
00:38:43,320 --> 00:38:46,840
but I'm the richest
and most powerful person on this plane."

670
00:38:47,920 --> 00:38:49,920
[string music continues]

671
00:39:06,720 --> 00:39:11,240
[Joachim] Trustor's cash reserves
were filled to the brim, nearly a billion.

672
00:39:11,320 --> 00:39:14,120
If I'd wanted to take the money and run,

673
00:39:14,640 --> 00:39:16,960
that would have been the moment to do it.

674
00:39:18,320 --> 00:39:19,840
But I had other ambitions.

675
00:39:21,120 --> 00:39:23,680
I wanted to build a corporate empire.

676
00:39:27,920 --> 00:39:30,240
[Karin] <i>Posener decided</i>
<i>London would be the site</i>

677
00:39:30,320 --> 00:39:31,880
<i>for this corporate empire.</i>

678
00:39:32,400 --> 00:39:35,280
<i>He'd figured out</i>
<i>that as long as he was living abroad,</i>

679
00:39:35,360 --> 00:39:38,000
<i>he could avoid</i>
<i>the probation service's supervision.</i>

680
00:39:42,040 --> 00:39:43,160
<i>To get established,</i>

681
00:39:43,240 --> 00:39:46,200
<i>Team Moyne enlisted the help</i>
<i>of a local operator.</i>

682
00:39:46,920 --> 00:39:47,920
[man] At lunchtime,

683
00:39:48,000 --> 00:39:50,600
I have a gin and dry martini.

684
00:39:50,680 --> 00:39:52,960
A little bit of gin…

685
00:39:53,560 --> 00:39:55,560
{\an8}Evening, whisky.

686
00:39:56,080 --> 00:39:58,520
{\an8}That's been my habit for about 50 years.

687
00:39:58,600 --> 00:40:00,000
Just a spot.

688
00:40:00,080 --> 00:40:01,080
Skol!

689
00:40:02,800 --> 00:40:05,680
[Karin] <i>The first task</i>
<i>was to find an office.</i>

690
00:40:06,320 --> 00:40:09,120
"We need the best office

691
00:40:09,200 --> 00:40:12,200
it is possible to have in London."

692
00:40:12,720 --> 00:40:15,080
"A helicopter pad, if possible."

693
00:40:15,160 --> 00:40:18,520
I'm thinking, "Who are these people?"

694
00:40:19,240 --> 00:40:20,800
Endless money.

695
00:40:23,400 --> 00:40:24,600
[Joachim] This was it.

696
00:40:25,920 --> 00:40:30,720
It was… the place to be
in London at that time.

697
00:40:31,720 --> 00:40:34,520
My office was that one,

698
00:40:34,600 --> 00:40:38,200
all the way at the top,
with its own terrace.

699
00:40:38,720 --> 00:40:40,240
We fought over it.

700
00:40:41,200 --> 00:40:43,480
Everyone wanted it, but I won.

701
00:40:44,600 --> 00:40:49,000
There was always, to me,
a little bit of an aura of mystery.

702
00:40:49,680 --> 00:40:52,360
{\an8}There was one, uh, room in particular,

703
00:40:52,440 --> 00:40:55,640
{\an8}I remember had to have treble walls.

704
00:40:56,680 --> 00:41:00,680
{\an8}[Joachim] From there, I'd listen
to the meeting going on next door,

705
00:41:01,280 --> 00:41:03,600
{\an8}directing Thomas over the phone,

706
00:41:03,680 --> 00:41:07,160
{\an8}so he would say
whatever I wanted him to say.

707
00:41:07,760 --> 00:41:09,640
{\an8}I asked Michael Wynne-Parker

708
00:41:09,720 --> 00:41:11,520
to help furnish the office.

709
00:41:11,600 --> 00:41:15,440
It had to be luxurious.
It had to be "investment banking."

710
00:41:15,520 --> 00:41:18,000
It had to be… top.

711
00:41:18,080 --> 00:41:22,320
And money was no object, so I set off.

712
00:41:22,400 --> 00:41:24,880
{\an8}["Still a Part of Me"
by The Minits playing]

713
00:41:29,960 --> 00:41:32,520
<i>♪ Yeah, oh… ♪</i>

714
00:41:34,200 --> 00:41:37,040
[Joachim] For me, it was important
that things looked right.

715
00:41:37,640 --> 00:41:41,720
I knew that would open new doors
and create opportunities.

716
00:41:41,800 --> 00:41:45,480
And then we discovered Napoleon's desk

717
00:41:46,000 --> 00:41:47,000
in Harrods.

718
00:41:47,520 --> 00:41:49,320
[Thomas] It was expensive as hell.

719
00:41:49,400 --> 00:41:52,040
Apparently, it came
from the Palace of Versailles.

720
00:41:52,560 --> 00:41:55,080
It was a really nice desk.
I wonder what happened to it.

721
00:41:55,680 --> 00:41:56,880
Poor Napoleon.

722
00:42:01,840 --> 00:42:04,720
[Karin] <i>Everyone on Team Moyne</i>
<i>took fees for their work.</i>

723
00:42:05,320 --> 00:42:07,160
{\an8}<i>That was not illegal in itself,</i>

724
00:42:07,240 --> 00:42:09,680
{\an8}<i>but the amounts were unusually high.</i>

725
00:42:11,440 --> 00:42:14,600
<i>They channelled large sums</i>
<i>through accounts in Gibraltar,</i>

726
00:42:14,680 --> 00:42:16,240
<i>Lichtenstein and Switzerland,</i>

727
00:42:16,320 --> 00:42:19,120
<i>and to girlfriends</i>
<i>and other family members.</i>

728
00:42:22,240 --> 00:42:24,480
<i>Before the summer half-year report,</i>

729
00:42:24,560 --> 00:42:27,160
<i>Team Moyne had to show</i>
<i>that no money was missing.</i>

730
00:42:27,680 --> 00:42:29,920
<i>The solution was a one-day loan.</i>

731
00:42:30,000 --> 00:42:32,840
<i>Window dressing from a bank in Luxembourg.</i>

732
00:42:33,720 --> 00:42:35,520
From the outside,

733
00:42:35,600 --> 00:42:38,480
it all seemed to be going very well.

734
00:42:39,840 --> 00:42:41,440
<i>♪ Still a part of me ♪</i>

735
00:42:42,360 --> 00:42:44,720
<i>♪ I can't break free ♪</i>

736
00:42:44,800 --> 00:42:46,440
<i>♪ Still a part of me ♪</i>

737
00:42:47,480 --> 00:42:49,800
<i>♪ I can't break free… ♪</i>

738
00:42:51,080 --> 00:42:54,000
[Karin] <i>After the deal,</i>
<i>they lived lavishly in London.</i>

739
00:42:54,080 --> 00:42:54,920
<i>Very lavishly.</i>

740
00:42:55,000 --> 00:42:57,880
<i>Joachim Posener was staying at a hotel.</i>

741
00:42:57,960 --> 00:43:01,720
<i>Thomas Jisander and Peter Mattsson</i>
<i>furnished a shared apartment.</i>

742
00:43:01,800 --> 00:43:04,440
<i>♪ You're still a part of me… ♪</i>

743
00:43:04,520 --> 00:43:07,480
[Thomas] It was a fantastic penthouse
with a wraparound terrace,

744
00:43:07,560 --> 00:43:09,680
with views over London and Hyde Park,

745
00:43:09,760 --> 00:43:12,880
with huge reception rooms
and golden faucets.

746
00:43:15,080 --> 00:43:17,240
My bedroom was entirely Versace.

747
00:43:17,320 --> 00:43:19,000
I was fully into the Versace thing.

748
00:43:19,080 --> 00:43:23,440
Versace bedspreads, Versace pillows,
Versace dressing gowns… Everything.

749
00:43:23,960 --> 00:43:25,440
Fantastic apartment.

750
00:43:28,680 --> 00:43:31,960
[Joachim] We split up for the summer
and took a break until the fall.

751
00:43:32,480 --> 00:43:34,440
Then we'd get to work.

752
00:43:35,800 --> 00:43:38,240
I told Thomas to keep a low profile.

753
00:43:38,800 --> 00:43:40,960
[whooping]

754
00:43:41,040 --> 00:43:42,040
[man] Whoa!

755
00:43:42,120 --> 00:43:43,560
[whooping]

756
00:43:43,640 --> 00:43:45,480
[laughing and cheering]

757
00:43:46,000 --> 00:43:48,040
Celebrating should be fun, not boring.

758
00:43:48,120 --> 00:43:50,960
And how do you have the most fun?
By doing whatever you want.

759
00:43:53,680 --> 00:43:56,280
We're now walking on Pampelonne Beach.

760
00:43:57,320 --> 00:43:58,840
27 years later.

761
00:43:59,480 --> 00:44:03,360
It's still a little exciting
to "walk the plank" again.

762
00:44:04,560 --> 00:44:05,560
It's kind of fun.

763
00:44:05,640 --> 00:44:08,040
Nerve-wracking,
but exciting at the same time.

764
00:44:09,160 --> 00:44:13,600
We're now approaching the very beach
where we partied after the fantastic deal.

765
00:44:14,120 --> 00:44:15,960
The bar was here.

766
00:44:16,680 --> 00:44:18,880
From somewhere over there to here.

767
00:44:19,520 --> 00:44:22,200
We did a great job.
I was well paid for my efforts.

768
00:44:22,280 --> 00:44:23,960
Money well-earned, I'd say.

769
00:44:24,560 --> 00:44:26,160
The bar was huge.

770
00:44:26,240 --> 00:44:27,600
We had to celebrate that.

771
00:44:27,680 --> 00:44:28,960
[whooping]

772
00:44:30,160 --> 00:44:32,320
Only proper way to do that
is with a yacht.

773
00:44:32,400 --> 00:44:34,400
Peter, wake up! Time to pop the cork.

774
00:44:34,920 --> 00:44:38,240
We boarded that boat in late June,
if I remember right.

775
00:44:38,320 --> 00:44:40,320
We had it for nearly two months.

776
00:44:43,240 --> 00:44:45,480
The boat was equipped
with a helicopter pad.

777
00:44:46,280 --> 00:44:49,840
It wasn't meant for flying 200 yards
from the boat to the beach.

778
00:44:49,920 --> 00:44:52,440
But that's why it was so fun to do it.

779
00:44:53,560 --> 00:44:57,040
We kept thinking we had to raise the bar.
"What are we going to do this time?"

780
00:44:58,240 --> 00:45:01,360
So I started dressing up
to keep things interesting.

781
00:45:01,440 --> 00:45:02,520
I put on

782
00:45:03,560 --> 00:45:06,880
a bra, high heels,
and those big Elton John glasses,

783
00:45:06,960 --> 00:45:10,240
and danced all over the boat
while blasting <i>Star Wars </i>music.

784
00:45:13,760 --> 00:45:15,520
This is the spot we flew in from.

785
00:45:16,280 --> 00:45:18,200
To there. Maybe 500 yards?

786
00:45:19,320 --> 00:45:20,160
Up in the air.

787
00:45:20,960 --> 00:45:23,520
The only place we could land
was on the roof of the bar.

788
00:45:25,120 --> 00:45:27,720
The bar at Voile Rouge
was made out of concrete.

789
00:45:27,800 --> 00:45:30,280
Four pillars and a very sturdy roof.

790
00:45:30,360 --> 00:45:32,560
That's where we landed
with the helicopter.

791
00:45:32,640 --> 00:45:35,880
But we didn't consider
how strong the rotor blades were.

792
00:45:35,960 --> 00:45:37,800
[imitates whirring rotor blades]

793
00:45:37,880 --> 00:45:41,480
We landed on the roof
and were gonna make a fantastic entrance.

794
00:45:41,560 --> 00:45:42,400
But…

795
00:45:42,480 --> 00:45:44,200
It blew everything away.

796
00:45:44,280 --> 00:45:47,760
People were sitting there eating lunch.
Everyone started running.

797
00:45:47,840 --> 00:45:49,120
[laughs]

798
00:45:49,200 --> 00:45:53,280
Everything was flying around.
People, food in their faces, bolognese…

799
00:45:53,360 --> 00:45:54,280
[imitates choking]

800
00:45:54,360 --> 00:45:56,600
…salmon, shrimp, you name it.

801
00:45:57,120 --> 00:45:59,440
All of it was all over everyone's faces.

802
00:45:59,960 --> 00:46:03,600
It looked like a war zone.
I thought, "What the hell do we do?"

803
00:46:03,680 --> 00:46:07,840
I came out of the helicopter riding high
but those people were going to kill us.

804
00:46:08,560 --> 00:46:09,880
To make up for the damage,

805
00:46:09,960 --> 00:46:11,920
I decided to order champagne.

806
00:46:12,000 --> 00:46:13,880
I ordered everything they had.

807
00:46:14,400 --> 00:46:16,040
"What do you mean, all of it?"

808
00:46:16,120 --> 00:46:17,160
"All of it!"

809
00:46:17,240 --> 00:46:19,200
["In My Mind" by Antiloop playing]

810
00:46:22,160 --> 00:46:24,800
[Joachim] The money
was burning a hole in his pocket.

811
00:46:26,080 --> 00:46:27,200
It was crazy.

812
00:46:27,280 --> 00:46:29,080
["In My Mind" continues playing]

813
00:46:32,880 --> 00:46:35,200
[Thomas] It must have been
one of the best summers

814
00:46:35,280 --> 00:46:39,800
for everyone who was on that beach
at Voile Rouge in July 1997.

815
00:46:40,440 --> 00:46:43,840
We got through 408 bottles of Cristal.

816
00:46:43,920 --> 00:46:45,440
<i>♪ In my mind, in my mind ♪</i>

817
00:46:45,520 --> 00:46:47,360
<i>♪ In my mind… ♪</i>

818
00:46:47,440 --> 00:46:49,480
{\an8}-[music ends]
-[makes fizzing sound]

819
00:46:52,040 --> 00:46:55,680
[Karin] <i>Meanwhile in Sweden,</i>
<i>at the much quieter Stockholm office,</i>

820
00:46:55,760 --> 00:46:59,560
<i>vice president Richard Djursén</i>
<i>was trying to hold things together.</i>

821
00:47:00,760 --> 00:47:04,520
I worked through the summer.
I was given a lot of strange tasks.

822
00:47:05,240 --> 00:47:07,840
They could be anything and everything.

823
00:47:07,920 --> 00:47:10,040
A lot of it was rather boring, though.

824
00:47:10,120 --> 00:47:13,360
I changed the locks on doors.
I bought a new fax machine.

825
00:47:13,440 --> 00:47:17,120
Plane tickets arrived for people
that had nothing to do with Trustor.

826
00:47:17,200 --> 00:47:18,080
{\an8}TO DO

827
00:47:18,160 --> 00:47:19,840
{\an8}I ran personal errands for them.

828
00:47:19,920 --> 00:47:20,760
{\an8}UNPAID BILLS

829
00:47:20,840 --> 00:47:24,200
{\an8}Thomas had an apartment in Vasastan,
not far from there.

830
00:47:24,280 --> 00:47:27,280
{\an8}I went there to collect his mail
and pay his bills.

831
00:47:27,920 --> 00:47:29,080
{\an8}With his money.

832
00:47:34,000 --> 00:47:35,360
It's starting to rain.

833
00:47:36,080 --> 00:47:38,240
I need to get these out of the rain

834
00:47:39,240 --> 00:47:41,880
because of all the pollen
in the air right now.

835
00:47:41,960 --> 00:47:46,000
But it's more of a hygiene issue.
I think it makes sense.

836
00:47:46,920 --> 00:47:48,600
Good exercise, too.

837
00:47:51,080 --> 00:47:52,800
Running back and forth.

838
00:47:52,880 --> 00:47:54,800
You don't have to do this in Marbella.

839
00:47:54,880 --> 00:47:57,640
Okay, I think that's it.
It's really coming down now.

840
00:47:59,560 --> 00:48:00,640
Oh my God.

841
00:48:02,360 --> 00:48:04,560
That summer,
I got a call from Richard Djursén.

842
00:48:04,640 --> 00:48:06,080
He was hysterical.

843
00:48:06,160 --> 00:48:09,720
"Jocke, Jocke, you have to do something.
It's going to be a disaster."

844
00:48:10,240 --> 00:48:15,040
He said that Thomas had ended up
in <i>Paris Match </i>magazine

845
00:48:15,120 --> 00:48:17,520
with his champagne parties.

846
00:48:18,040 --> 00:48:19,280
So I called him.

847
00:48:20,240 --> 00:48:22,320
But there was no stopping Thomas.

848
00:48:25,680 --> 00:48:29,200
[Karin] <i>You couldn't accuse them</i>
<i>of being boring on the French Riviera.</i>

849
00:48:29,280 --> 00:48:32,960
<i>Thomas Jisander was given the nickname</i>
<i>"Mr. No Limit."</i>

850
00:48:33,040 --> 00:48:37,880
<i>Peter Mattsson and Thomas Jisander</i>
<i>each bought a Ferrari on a whim.</i>

851
00:48:39,640 --> 00:48:42,160
[Thomas] One blue, a Ferrari F355,

852
00:48:42,240 --> 00:48:44,120
and an identical red one.

853
00:48:44,200 --> 00:48:46,600
They were around one million francs.

854
00:48:47,200 --> 00:48:50,160
We paid in cash,
got in the cars and drove off.

855
00:48:50,240 --> 00:48:51,760
[engine revs loudly]

856
00:48:53,480 --> 00:48:55,120
I never saw that car again.

857
00:48:56,920 --> 00:48:58,760
I had that Ferrari for 15 minutes.

858
00:48:58,840 --> 00:49:01,760
I don't know where it ended up.
I left it somewhere.

859
00:49:02,360 --> 00:49:04,080
So much happened that summer.

860
00:49:04,720 --> 00:49:06,400
We had one car left.

861
00:49:06,920 --> 00:49:11,680
So we decided to drive down together
to the Versace store in Saint-Tropez.

862
00:49:12,720 --> 00:49:15,640
I was horrified when they told me.

863
00:49:16,440 --> 00:49:18,960
It was the exact opposite
of what you should do

864
00:49:19,040 --> 00:49:22,640
if you've just bought a company
with its own money.

865
00:49:22,720 --> 00:49:24,640
You don't want to draw attention.

866
00:49:24,720 --> 00:49:27,480
We had this unspoken competition going
the whole time.

867
00:49:27,560 --> 00:49:29,520
"The one who has most toys
when he dies wins."

868
00:49:29,600 --> 00:49:30,480
More or less.

869
00:49:30,560 --> 00:49:32,440
I would never in my wildest imagination

870
00:49:32,520 --> 00:49:35,800
have thought that anyone
could be so reckless.

871
00:49:36,320 --> 00:49:38,280
I'd underestimated Thomas.

872
00:49:38,360 --> 00:49:42,560
[Thomas] In 1997, that summer,
the Versace store was here.

873
00:49:42,640 --> 00:49:45,200
We rolled up from over here.

874
00:49:45,720 --> 00:49:46,920
That's where I stopped.

875
00:49:47,000 --> 00:49:48,640
[imitates screeching brakes]

876
00:49:48,720 --> 00:49:52,400
I dropped Peter off,
and as he's getting out, he says,

877
00:49:52,480 --> 00:49:56,120
"There won't be a single thing left
in the store by the time you come in."

878
00:49:56,840 --> 00:49:59,920
He walked straight into the store.
We'd had a few drinks.

879
00:50:00,720 --> 00:50:03,080
"There'll be nothing left for you at all."

880
00:50:03,640 --> 00:50:06,160
He bought everything in every size.

881
00:50:06,760 --> 00:50:07,840
That set me off.

882
00:50:08,360 --> 00:50:10,120
"How do I top this?"

883
00:50:10,680 --> 00:50:12,640
So I told them that I wanted the rest.

884
00:50:13,280 --> 00:50:14,640
"There's nothing left, sir."

885
00:50:15,160 --> 00:50:17,000
"I'll take the checkout counter,

886
00:50:17,080 --> 00:50:19,520
the cash register,
the changing room doors,

887
00:50:19,600 --> 00:50:22,280
the drapes, curtains
and the light fixtures."

888
00:50:22,360 --> 00:50:24,680
"Unscrew everything, the whole store."

889
00:50:25,280 --> 00:50:27,680
Electrical wires were hanging everywhere.

890
00:50:27,760 --> 00:50:31,360
It was completely gutted, like a grenade
had been thrown into the place.

891
00:50:31,960 --> 00:50:34,440
Then the owner came out
with a screwdriver.

892
00:50:34,520 --> 00:50:36,360
There was a Medusa here,

893
00:50:36,440 --> 00:50:38,920
cut in half,
so you could open the door like this.

894
00:50:39,440 --> 00:50:40,440
It was beautiful.

895
00:50:41,240 --> 00:50:42,960
So he unscrewed the handles.

896
00:50:43,480 --> 00:50:45,160
That was it. Nothing left.

897
00:50:45,680 --> 00:50:46,760
Ransacked.

898
00:50:48,720 --> 00:50:52,520
[Karin] How much did you spend
in total, the summer of 1997?

899
00:50:53,080 --> 00:50:54,240
Oy.

900
00:50:54,320 --> 00:50:56,800
I don't know. I can do a rough estimate.

901
00:50:56,880 --> 00:51:01,640
The boat cost three, four million a week,
plus fuel and that sort of thing.

902
00:51:01,720 --> 00:51:02,600
Um…

903
00:51:03,840 --> 00:51:06,160
We had it for eight weeks, so…

904
00:51:06,680 --> 00:51:08,800
uh… 50 million, maybe?

905
00:51:09,400 --> 00:51:10,920
Something like that. 40?

906
00:51:14,320 --> 00:51:16,760
-[Karin] Was it worth it?
-Yes, it was.

907
00:51:20,040 --> 00:51:23,000
[Karin] How much were you paid
in total from Trustor?

908
00:51:23,080 --> 00:51:26,360
I don't know the exact figure.
I'm so old now, I can't remember.

909
00:51:28,720 --> 00:51:29,600
[man sighs]

910
00:51:30,400 --> 00:51:34,520
If these guys hadn't been gallivanting
around the French Riviera like fools,

911
00:51:34,600 --> 00:51:36,920
they probably would've got away with it.

912
00:51:38,320 --> 00:51:41,360
[Karin] <i>This is financial veteran</i>
<i>Björn Björnsson.</i>

913
00:51:41,440 --> 00:51:44,240
{\an8}<i>He's been called</i>
<i>the Terminator of the business world,</i>

914
00:51:44,840 --> 00:51:46,800
{\an8}<i>the industry's own sheriff.</i>

915
00:51:47,320 --> 00:51:49,080
I think they all wanted this.

916
00:51:49,160 --> 00:51:50,640
Money, money, money.

917
00:51:50,720 --> 00:51:52,120
But here's the problem…

918
00:51:52,200 --> 00:51:53,400
Money talks.

919
00:51:54,480 --> 00:51:56,920
That might make you look the other way.

920
00:51:59,480 --> 00:52:03,280
[Karin] <i>Björn Björnsson ended up</i>
<i>taking on more roles than anyone expected.</i>

921
00:52:04,120 --> 00:52:06,760
<i>His first role</i>
<i>was as a board member of Trustor</i>

922
00:52:06,840 --> 00:52:09,040
<i>when the actual purchase was made.</i>

923
00:52:10,280 --> 00:52:13,920
When Lord Moyne stood
as owner of the A shares in Trustor,

924
00:52:14,000 --> 00:52:16,080
I assumed they'd been paid for.

925
00:52:17,720 --> 00:52:19,280
But that wasn't the case.

926
00:52:21,640 --> 00:52:25,920
You can't take 241 million
without it being noticed.

927
00:52:26,440 --> 00:52:28,560
Sooner or later, you get caught.

928
00:52:29,280 --> 00:52:32,160
There had to be more to the plan.

929
00:52:32,720 --> 00:52:33,880
A master plan.

930
00:52:39,920 --> 00:52:42,360
[Joachim] My long-term plan
was to build up

931
00:52:42,440 --> 00:52:44,720
and own a corporate empire.

932
00:52:45,240 --> 00:52:49,680
I was going to accomplish that
with a classic pyramid owner structure.

933
00:52:50,240 --> 00:52:53,760
One company that owns another company
that owns a third.

934
00:52:54,280 --> 00:52:56,960
If the first company was Trustor
at one billion,

935
00:52:57,040 --> 00:52:59,760
and the second company
was worth five billion,

936
00:52:59,840 --> 00:53:02,680
then the third could be worth ten billion.

937
00:53:03,200 --> 00:53:05,080
After acquiring Trustor,

938
00:53:05,160 --> 00:53:08,960
I used its money
to make my next acquisition.

939
00:53:09,040 --> 00:53:10,240
THE SPORTS DIVISION
WILSON

940
00:53:10,320 --> 00:53:13,680
First, I tried Wilson,
the international sports brand.

941
00:53:13,760 --> 00:53:16,240
But the money came in four days late,

942
00:53:16,320 --> 00:53:17,880
so the deal fell through.

943
00:53:18,400 --> 00:53:23,520
That's how close I was to getting
the next company in place in my pyramid.

944
00:53:23,600 --> 00:53:25,600
[tense music playing]

945
00:53:29,800 --> 00:53:32,200
[Karin] <i>Team Moyne</i>
<i>would acquire new companies</i>

946
00:53:32,280 --> 00:53:34,560
<i>and sell off Trustor's assets.</i>

947
00:53:36,240 --> 00:53:39,680
[Joachim] When we got back to the office
in London after the summer,

948
00:53:39,760 --> 00:53:42,400
everything was completely different.

949
00:53:42,960 --> 00:53:44,120
[Thomas] Business as usual.

950
00:53:44,200 --> 00:53:46,840
It was time to dust ourselves off
and wash the suits.

951
00:53:47,840 --> 00:53:50,720
We had to get back to work
and start looking for new deals.

952
00:53:52,960 --> 00:53:55,240
From my apartment in London to the office,

953
00:53:55,320 --> 00:53:59,320
I travelled every morning
by private chauffeur, in two cars.

954
00:53:59,400 --> 00:54:00,760
I rode in the front one

955
00:54:00,840 --> 00:54:03,360
and my briefcase travelled
in the one behind me.

956
00:54:05,920 --> 00:54:09,720
When it came to showing up to work
on time, I wasn't overly concerned.

957
00:54:12,000 --> 00:54:14,920
[Joachim] Thomas arrived on Tuesday
and went home on Thursday.

958
00:54:15,000 --> 00:54:16,520
We argued the whole time.

959
00:54:17,160 --> 00:54:19,440
Thomas had been my loyal henchman.

960
00:54:19,520 --> 00:54:23,040
He'd always done everything for me,
and it was perfect.

961
00:54:23,760 --> 00:54:26,480
Then… he lost his mind.

962
00:54:26,560 --> 00:54:28,160
He sided with Peter Mattsson.

963
00:54:28,240 --> 00:54:30,800
Suddenly it was Thomas and Peter
who were a team,

964
00:54:30,880 --> 00:54:33,240
when it used to be Thomas and me.

965
00:54:33,320 --> 00:54:34,440
I was losing him.

966
00:54:34,520 --> 00:54:36,600
My focus was on finding a solution

967
00:54:36,680 --> 00:54:39,520
that would make
my ownership of Trustor legal.

968
00:54:39,600 --> 00:54:43,360
Annual accounts were due on December 31st.

969
00:54:43,440 --> 00:54:46,200
It was September. I had four months.

970
00:54:47,560 --> 00:54:51,600
So I needed to keep Thomas
somewhat… in check.

971
00:54:53,000 --> 00:54:58,080
I think he was jealous that he was not
living it up in high society like I was.

972
00:54:58,160 --> 00:54:59,920
He wanted to do what I was doing.

973
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:01,960
If I said A, he said B,

974
00:55:02,040 --> 00:55:04,960
just to make a point
that he also was important.

975
00:55:07,120 --> 00:55:08,880
My entire control of Trustor

976
00:55:08,960 --> 00:55:13,200
depended on Thomas being between me
and the rest of the world.

977
00:55:13,280 --> 00:55:17,000
I had entrusted him
with being the one who held the money.

978
00:55:17,080 --> 00:55:19,720
The money sat in his account, not mine.

979
00:55:19,800 --> 00:55:21,640
He suddenly had the power.

980
00:55:22,800 --> 00:55:27,320
We started shouting at each other,
like children, in front of everyone.

981
00:55:27,400 --> 00:55:30,720
All of a sudden, my hired lackeys
wanted everything to be put to a vote

982
00:55:30,800 --> 00:55:32,080
and decided as a group.

983
00:55:32,680 --> 00:55:35,600
Lord Moyne and Lindsay Smallbone
sat on the board.

984
00:55:36,120 --> 00:55:37,720
I had no role at all.

985
00:55:38,480 --> 00:55:44,880
Then Thomas and Peter
were busy trying to stop a journalist

986
00:55:44,960 --> 00:55:46,200
who'd turned up.

987
00:55:46,840 --> 00:55:50,200
I didn't think much of that at all.
He just wanted to ask a few questions.

988
00:55:50,280 --> 00:55:52,320
I think that's normal after a large deal.

989
00:55:52,400 --> 00:55:54,400
[typewriter clacking]

990
00:55:55,480 --> 00:55:57,080
[Gunnar] It was a coincidence.

991
00:55:57,160 --> 00:55:58,960
I was very new at Svenska Dagbladet.

992
00:55:59,040 --> 00:56:01,080
I was given various assignments.

993
00:56:01,760 --> 00:56:03,840
Lord Moyne had just bought Trustor.

994
00:56:04,880 --> 00:56:08,040
We came up with the idea
of doing an interview with him

995
00:56:08,120 --> 00:56:10,640
and trying to profile him.
So I got started.

996
00:56:14,040 --> 00:56:16,360
But when I called Trustor the next day,

997
00:56:16,440 --> 00:56:17,560
he wasn't there.

998
00:56:18,320 --> 00:56:20,920
I got put in touch with Richard Djursén,

999
00:56:21,000 --> 00:56:24,440
who promised to set something up for me.

1000
00:56:25,120 --> 00:56:26,480
[Richard] I called Team Moyne,

1001
00:56:26,560 --> 00:56:30,520
and they came up with
one reason after another

1002
00:56:30,600 --> 00:56:33,440
to postpone the interview again and again.

1003
00:56:33,520 --> 00:56:36,320
The journalist was irritated,
to put it mildly.

1004
00:56:37,280 --> 00:56:40,200
At that time, it didn't occur to me
that it could be a fraud.

1005
00:56:40,720 --> 00:56:42,000
I just wanted insight.

1006
00:56:42,080 --> 00:56:45,280
The more he discovered,
the more curious he became.

1007
00:56:45,360 --> 00:56:49,240
Over time, I started to feel
that something wasn't right.

1008
00:56:50,640 --> 00:56:53,760
I had doubts about
whether Lord Moyne had any money.

1009
00:56:53,840 --> 00:56:57,360
Instead of the prominent businessman
that he made himself out to be,

1010
00:56:57,440 --> 00:57:01,880
I began to suspect that he might be
the black sheep of the Guinness family.

1011
00:57:03,360 --> 00:57:07,440
In my research, I had also learned about
Peter Mattsson's involvement in a company

1012
00:57:07,520 --> 00:57:11,120
that had swindled wealthy Englishmen
out of their fortunes.

1013
00:57:11,720 --> 00:57:13,840
Lindsay Smallbone had also run companies

1014
00:57:13,920 --> 00:57:16,240
and then taken money
for his own personal use

1015
00:57:16,320 --> 00:57:17,440
and things like that.

1016
00:57:18,800 --> 00:57:20,480
A band of thieves, basically.

1017
00:57:20,560 --> 00:57:22,520
I had no idea about any of this.

1018
00:57:22,600 --> 00:57:25,680
Their skeletons
came tumbling out of the closet,

1019
00:57:25,760 --> 00:57:29,360
all the things they'd concealed from me
in order to be part of the deal.

1020
00:57:30,880 --> 00:57:33,760
The irony is, if they had
given me an interview the next day

1021
00:57:33,840 --> 00:57:35,440
when I first called,

1022
00:57:36,160 --> 00:57:39,720
there wouldn't have been a Trustor affair.
At least, not because of me.

1023
00:57:44,080 --> 00:57:47,680
[Karin] <i>Coincidences can set off</i>
<i>a chain reaction of events.</i>

1024
00:57:47,760 --> 00:57:52,080
<i>At the same time as the journalist</i>
<i>started digging into the deal,</i>

1025
00:57:52,160 --> 00:57:55,560
<i>a British private investigator</i>
<i>received a new assignment.</i>

1026
00:57:56,960 --> 00:57:59,000
{\an8}For the last maybe 35 years or so,

1027
00:57:59,080 --> 00:58:00,880
{\an8}I've been a fraud investigator.

1028
00:58:00,960 --> 00:58:02,120
{\an8}It's not rocket science.

1029
00:58:02,640 --> 00:58:04,840
It's like cooking, anyone can do it.

1030
00:58:06,920 --> 00:58:09,360
[Karin] <i>His assignment was to dig up dirt</i>

1031
00:58:09,440 --> 00:58:12,120
<i>on one of the parties in a legal dispute.</i>

1032
00:58:12,200 --> 00:58:14,840
<i>And that person happened to be…</i>

1033
00:58:15,440 --> 00:58:19,160
<i>Lindsay Smallbone, Trustor's new CEO.</i>

1034
00:58:20,680 --> 00:58:21,960
The client said,

1035
00:58:22,040 --> 00:58:25,600
"I want to look into Lindsay Smallbone.
I have a bone to pick with him."

1036
00:58:25,680 --> 00:58:27,720
"I'd like you to see who he really is,

1037
00:58:27,800 --> 00:58:30,280
because I think he's a cheat and a crook."

1038
00:58:30,360 --> 00:58:33,880
So we did the background search
on Lindsay Smallbone,

1039
00:58:33,960 --> 00:58:36,040
and found out that Lindsay was

1040
00:58:36,120 --> 00:58:39,680
a director of a company in Sweden
called Trustor AB.

1041
00:58:39,760 --> 00:58:42,200
So let's see what this company

1042
00:58:42,280 --> 00:58:44,360
he's a managing director of is.

1043
00:58:45,160 --> 00:58:47,840
I'm flicking through this file of Trustor.

1044
00:58:47,920 --> 00:58:51,680
There was something
just didn't seem right in that paperwork.

1045
00:58:52,240 --> 00:58:57,280
It looked like the payment was going
to the original owner Norberg afterwards.

1046
00:58:57,360 --> 00:58:59,400
And I thought, "Hang on a second."

1047
00:58:59,920 --> 00:59:01,440
"It doesn't make sense,

1048
00:59:01,520 --> 00:59:04,200
because you shouldn't be in control
of the company

1049
00:59:04,280 --> 00:59:05,760
and then pay the person."

1050
00:59:05,840 --> 00:59:09,200
"Something's wrong with this company.
Something's really wrong."

1051
00:59:09,800 --> 00:59:12,000
[tense electronic music playing]

1052
00:59:13,040 --> 00:59:15,960
[Karin] <i>The walls are closing in</i>
<i>from every direction.</i>

1053
00:59:16,040 --> 00:59:18,200
<i>An investigative journalist,</i>

1054
00:59:18,280 --> 00:59:21,120
<i>and, on another front,</i>
<i>a private investigator,</i>

1055
00:59:21,200 --> 00:59:23,760
<i>and, on top of that, the police.</i>

1056
00:59:24,320 --> 00:59:26,760
<i>Because on the same day</i>
<i>the private investigator</i>

1057
00:59:26,840 --> 00:59:29,000
<i>stumbled across</i>
<i>the information about Trustor,</i>

1058
00:59:29,080 --> 00:59:31,640
<i>he had a meeting</i>
<i>with the financial crimes unit</i>

1059
00:59:31,720 --> 00:59:33,680
<i>on a completely different matter.</i>

1060
00:59:35,120 --> 00:59:37,920
It was Friday, October 17th, 1997.

1061
00:59:39,440 --> 00:59:43,600
The meeting to see Jochum Söderström
was nothing to do with Trustor.

1062
00:59:43,680 --> 00:59:46,040
That's important.
I just had it on my mind.

1063
00:59:47,280 --> 00:59:49,520
[Karin] <i>That day,</i>
<i>an overly long phone call</i>

1064
00:59:49,600 --> 00:59:54,600
<i>would accidentally cause one of Sweden's</i>
<i>largest police investigations.</i>

1065
00:59:55,920 --> 00:59:59,160
[Nigel] I arrived early,
but Jochum, I could see in one office,

1066
00:59:59,240 --> 01:00:00,520
was on the telephone.

1067
01:00:00,600 --> 01:00:02,400
I directed him to my colleague.

1068
01:00:02,920 --> 01:00:05,200
Nigel went over, they started talking,

1069
01:00:05,280 --> 01:00:07,200
and I continued my call.

1070
01:00:07,280 --> 01:00:09,560
[Nigel] I was being shown this paperwork,

1071
01:00:09,640 --> 01:00:12,920
very privileged to see
what they were gathering intelligence on.

1072
01:00:13,000 --> 01:00:15,400
And I just said, "This is small stuff."

1073
01:00:16,560 --> 01:00:19,160
"Big stuff is actually already happening,

1074
01:00:19,240 --> 01:00:22,160
but it's happening in open space,
on the stock exchange."

1075
01:00:22,960 --> 01:00:25,280
[Jochum] I can see
they're getting worked up.

1076
01:00:25,880 --> 01:00:27,080
At that moment,

1077
01:00:27,160 --> 01:00:29,440
Jochum had finished his phone call.

1078
01:00:29,520 --> 01:00:33,320
He stood there and went, "Nigel,
which company are you talking about?"

1079
01:00:33,880 --> 01:00:36,760
He was able to tell me
it was the investment company Trustor.

1080
01:00:36,840 --> 01:00:41,680
Everything happened between
about 12:30 and six in the afternoon.

1081
01:00:41,760 --> 01:00:43,400
We're talking about six hours.

1082
01:00:44,280 --> 01:00:45,320
Then I was out.

1083
01:00:45,840 --> 01:00:48,440
It was sheer coincidence
that we learned about this.

1084
01:00:49,640 --> 01:00:53,440
This became the starting gun
for us to launch the intelligence work,

1085
01:00:53,960 --> 01:00:56,800
and work towards
a preliminary investigation.

1086
01:00:59,720 --> 01:01:02,480
Nigel also told us there was a journalist

1087
01:01:02,560 --> 01:01:04,960
who had already been in contact with them.

1088
01:01:05,480 --> 01:01:08,840
So I decided we should call him in
to see what he knew.

1089
01:01:09,400 --> 01:01:10,920
[Gunnar] So we made a deal.

1090
01:01:11,000 --> 01:01:14,120
"I give you information
and you give me information."

1091
01:01:20,440 --> 01:01:23,680
I knew a very damning newspaper article
was going to come out

1092
01:01:23,760 --> 01:01:25,080
at the end of October.

1093
01:01:26,640 --> 01:01:31,320
But I didn't know the police
had started an investigation.

1094
01:01:32,080 --> 01:01:37,680
At the time, I'd already booked a trip
with my daughter and my girlfriend.

1095
01:01:37,760 --> 01:01:42,000
It was the first time my daughter and I
would be able to go somewhere together.

1096
01:01:42,080 --> 01:01:45,800
Because I'd been in prison,
I'd missed four of her five years.

1097
01:01:45,880 --> 01:01:48,240
Those important years of changing diapers

1098
01:01:48,320 --> 01:01:51,400
and being there to comfort her
when she needed it.

1099
01:01:51,480 --> 01:01:54,560
This was our chance to get a fresh start.

1100
01:01:56,360 --> 01:01:58,280
So I decided to go anyway.

1101
01:01:58,360 --> 01:02:01,120
We went to Barbados for a week.

1102
01:02:05,520 --> 01:02:07,440
[foreboding music playing]

1103
01:02:07,520 --> 01:02:09,680
It was important to work quickly.

1104
01:02:10,360 --> 01:02:14,280
We had to focus on what happened
and who did what.

1105
01:02:15,080 --> 01:02:17,360
It didn't take long until we discovered

1106
01:02:17,440 --> 01:02:20,280
that Lord Moyne was flat broke.

1107
01:02:21,480 --> 01:02:22,520
At the same time,

1108
01:02:22,600 --> 01:02:24,280
we looked into the Swedes,

1109
01:02:24,360 --> 01:02:26,960
Peter Mattsson and Thomas Jisander.

1110
01:02:27,480 --> 01:02:29,760
Did they perhaps have any credit cards?

1111
01:02:30,280 --> 01:02:31,320
Yes, they did.

1112
01:02:32,120 --> 01:02:36,040
A massive amount of money
had been spent in Saint-Tropez,

1113
01:02:36,120 --> 01:02:38,080
buying cases of champagne,

1114
01:02:38,160 --> 01:02:41,080
renting helicopters, renting a boat.

1115
01:02:41,840 --> 01:02:43,600
Really living it up out there.

1116
01:02:44,800 --> 01:02:47,080
We knew we were on to something here.

1117
01:02:48,360 --> 01:02:51,160
We contacted the central bank of Sweden

1118
01:02:51,240 --> 01:02:53,360
to see whether any more money

1119
01:02:53,440 --> 01:02:54,840
had gone abroad.

1120
01:02:55,360 --> 01:02:58,400
We had discovered that over 600 million

1121
01:02:58,480 --> 01:03:00,800
had been paid out to a mysterious account

1122
01:03:00,880 --> 01:03:03,200
at Barclays Bank in London.

1123
01:03:03,720 --> 01:03:08,440
They also told us that the account balance
was almost zeroed out.

1124
01:03:09,160 --> 01:03:10,160
This was serious.

1125
01:03:10,760 --> 01:03:12,520
[tense string music playing]

1126
01:03:15,080 --> 01:03:18,880
{\an8}[Karin] <i>Everyone on Team Moyne is abroad</i>
<i>as police and the journalist dig deeper.</i>

1127
01:03:18,960 --> 01:03:21,360
{\an8}<i>Piece by piece, the plan was uncovered.</i>

1128
01:03:25,560 --> 01:03:27,240
{\an8}-[music ends]
-[typewriter clacking]

1129
01:03:27,320 --> 01:03:30,680
[Gunnar] There was a lot of back and forth
before the article was published.

1130
01:03:32,120 --> 01:03:32,960
[sighs]

1131
01:03:33,040 --> 01:03:34,400
Were the facts correct?

1132
01:03:34,480 --> 01:03:38,120
We had to double-check everything
and be absolutely sure.

1133
01:03:40,280 --> 01:03:42,920
[Richard] Then Gunnar Lindstedt
published his article.

1134
01:03:45,720 --> 01:03:47,040
And that was it.

1135
01:03:47,560 --> 01:03:51,000
THE POLICE INVESTIGATES TRUSTOR DEALS

1136
01:03:51,080 --> 01:03:53,320
{\an8}POWER STRUGGLE INSTIGATED LORD

1137
01:03:53,400 --> 01:03:56,720
PEOPLE INVOLVED IN THE TRUSTOR PLOT

1138
01:03:56,800 --> 01:03:59,000
Team Moyne began to panic in London.

1139
01:03:59,520 --> 01:04:03,800
They were demanding answers to questions
that I can't even remember.

1140
01:04:03,880 --> 01:04:07,000
We went back and forth.
I was asked to look into this, deny that.

1141
01:04:07,080 --> 01:04:08,400
All sorts of stuff.

1142
01:04:10,240 --> 01:04:13,840
[Jochum] We went to the Trustor offices.
Richard Djursén was there.

1143
01:04:14,880 --> 01:04:17,280
We sat down to talk to Djursén.

1144
01:04:17,880 --> 01:04:20,560
After a while,
he just broke down completely.

1145
01:04:22,000 --> 01:04:25,160
We needed to find
the person who was in charge of this deal.

1146
01:04:29,600 --> 01:04:31,880
Three people
were part of the Lord's entourage.

1147
01:04:31,960 --> 01:04:34,120
Peter Mattsson and Thomas Jisander,

1148
01:04:34,200 --> 01:04:36,040
and then there was Joe Falk.

1149
01:04:36,560 --> 01:04:38,320
We knew nothing about him.

1150
01:04:38,960 --> 01:04:42,240
[Gunnar] According to my sources,
this was a key character.

1151
01:04:43,200 --> 01:04:44,880
Who is Joe Falk?

1152
01:04:44,960 --> 01:04:47,640
[intriguing music playing]

1153
01:04:48,760 --> 01:04:51,520
[Jochum] He clearly held
a prominent position.

1154
01:04:54,240 --> 01:04:56,000
Who was Joe Falk?

1155
01:04:57,440 --> 01:04:58,560
EUROCARD - ADDITIONAL ORDER

1156
01:04:58,640 --> 01:05:02,480
That evening,
Richard Djursén calls and tells us,

1157
01:05:03,040 --> 01:05:05,520
"Check out Thomas Jisander's cousin."

1158
01:05:08,040 --> 01:05:09,800
We checked the criminal records.

1159
01:05:10,400 --> 01:05:11,960
And who did we find?

1160
01:05:12,480 --> 01:05:13,680
Joe Falk.

1161
01:05:14,440 --> 01:05:15,880
His real name

1162
01:05:16,440 --> 01:05:18,160
was Joachim Posener.

1163
01:05:18,680 --> 01:05:21,160
[intriguing music intensifies]

1164
01:05:26,360 --> 01:05:28,240
[Joachim] As I prepared
for the Trustor deal,

1165
01:05:29,040 --> 01:05:30,840
I sometimes used

1166
01:05:31,360 --> 01:05:33,240
made-up names,

1167
01:05:33,320 --> 01:05:35,040
such as Joakim Rolfsson,

1168
01:05:35,120 --> 01:05:36,560
Ralph Jobe,

1169
01:05:36,640 --> 01:05:38,080
and Joe Falk.

1170
01:05:39,040 --> 01:05:43,720
I didn't want anyone to associate
the name Joachim Posener with Trustor.

1171
01:05:45,360 --> 01:05:48,040
[music softens]

1172
01:05:48,120 --> 01:05:49,280
While I'm in Barbados,

1173
01:05:51,000 --> 01:05:52,880
my life falls apart.

1174
01:05:54,320 --> 01:05:57,880
I remember I was having lunch
on a sundeck by the pool.

1175
01:05:58,920 --> 01:06:00,360
A waiter comes up to me.

1176
01:06:00,440 --> 01:06:02,880
"Mr. Posener, there's a call for you."

1177
01:06:02,960 --> 01:06:04,480
He points at a telephone there.

1178
01:06:04,560 --> 01:06:07,560
It was back when we had those on the wall.

1179
01:06:08,160 --> 01:06:11,320
I expected bad news,
but… nothing like that.

1180
01:06:12,120 --> 01:06:14,320
I pick up the phone. It's Thomas.

1181
01:06:14,400 --> 01:06:15,720
-Hello?
-[Joachim] Saying…

1182
01:06:15,800 --> 01:06:17,200
"Jocke,

1183
01:06:17,880 --> 01:06:19,200
listen carefully."

1184
01:06:20,800 --> 01:06:22,360
"The police raided us."

1185
01:06:22,440 --> 01:06:24,440
[tense music playing]

1186
01:06:26,160 --> 01:06:28,400
"They've launched
a preliminary investigation."

1187
01:06:28,920 --> 01:06:30,160
"What's that?" I asked.

1188
01:06:30,680 --> 01:06:32,880
He said, "Well, it's not good."

1189
01:06:32,960 --> 01:06:34,600
[chuckles]

1190
01:06:35,480 --> 01:06:37,160
No, it wasn't.

1191
01:06:39,160 --> 01:06:41,280
I knew it was over right away.

1192
01:06:42,240 --> 01:06:43,320
We had to act quickly.

1193
01:06:43,400 --> 01:06:45,640
There was a risk
that the money might disappear

1194
01:06:45,720 --> 01:06:47,960
once they realised what was happening.

1195
01:06:48,560 --> 01:06:51,280
Time was up.
The police were banging on the door.

1196
01:06:51,360 --> 01:06:52,920
They were already inside.

1197
01:06:55,160 --> 01:06:56,880
I had one image in my head.

1198
01:06:57,400 --> 01:06:58,680
Norrtälje.

1199
01:07:00,320 --> 01:07:02,000
I had a video camera.

1200
01:07:02,560 --> 01:07:03,720
And, uh,

1201
01:07:04,240 --> 01:07:08,280
my girlfriend was filming me
at the world's most amazing restaurant.

1202
01:07:08,360 --> 01:07:11,600
My daughter said something to me
and I answered her,

1203
01:07:11,680 --> 01:07:13,200
but we talked past each other.

1204
01:07:13,280 --> 01:07:15,560
I was just… not there.

1205
01:07:16,080 --> 01:07:17,320
It was over.

1206
01:07:19,120 --> 01:07:20,240
[clears throat]

1207
01:07:23,560 --> 01:07:25,760
A lot of things were happening at once.

1208
01:07:25,840 --> 01:07:28,760
So I left Barbados on October 31st.

1209
01:07:29,320 --> 01:07:33,240
That same day,
Svenska Dagbladet published their article

1210
01:07:33,320 --> 01:07:35,320
and the police raided Trustor.

1211
01:07:35,400 --> 01:07:40,000
Thomas was waiting for me at Heathrow
when we arrived from Barbados.

1212
01:07:40,080 --> 01:07:42,400
I sent my girlfriend and daughter
back to Sweden.

1213
01:07:42,480 --> 01:07:44,880
My girlfriend was supposed to
sort out a few things

1214
01:07:44,960 --> 01:07:47,000
and then come back to London.

1215
01:07:47,080 --> 01:07:50,320
One of the things
was to go to Thomas's place,

1216
01:07:50,400 --> 01:07:52,200
where I'd left a few things,

1217
01:07:53,280 --> 01:07:54,920
and get rid of them.

1218
01:07:55,880 --> 01:07:58,120
She succeeded, partly.

1219
01:07:58,800 --> 01:08:00,640
She left a notebook behind.

1220
01:08:04,000 --> 01:08:07,160
[Karin] <i>So when the police searched</i>
<i>Thomas Jisander's home,</i>

1221
01:08:07,240 --> 01:08:12,040
<i>they found several pieces of information</i>
<i>that linked Joachim Posener to the deal.</i>

1222
01:08:14,200 --> 01:08:15,600
In Jisander's apartment,

1223
01:08:15,680 --> 01:08:17,960
we found documents
and plans for the crime,

1224
01:08:18,040 --> 01:08:19,840
detailing how they did it.

1225
01:08:20,440 --> 01:08:22,120
HOW HE PLANNED TO TAKE OVER TRUSTOR

1226
01:08:22,640 --> 01:08:27,040
They also confirmed
that Joachim Posener was the mastermind.

1227
01:08:29,520 --> 01:08:32,160
[Joachim] It came to light
that 400 million was missing

1228
01:08:32,240 --> 01:08:33,920
from Trustor's accounts.

1229
01:08:35,960 --> 01:08:37,960
Thomas knew a few people in Geneva.

1230
01:08:38,560 --> 01:08:41,920
"They've got a solution, Jocke."
And off we went.

1231
01:08:42,640 --> 01:08:43,840
LE RICHEMOND - GENEVA

1232
01:08:43,920 --> 01:08:45,920
Thomas had arranged a meeting

1233
01:08:46,000 --> 01:08:48,600
with the mafia's bankers.

1234
01:08:49,280 --> 01:08:51,480
Both were called Ricardo,

1235
01:08:51,560 --> 01:08:53,360
and they were both Italians.

1236
01:08:53,440 --> 01:08:55,280
They had bodyguards with them.

1237
01:08:55,800 --> 01:08:57,120
I realised straightaway

1238
01:08:57,200 --> 01:09:00,920
that they were involved
in organised crime in Italy.

1239
01:09:02,800 --> 01:09:06,200
I was under the impression
that they would present a solution

1240
01:09:06,280 --> 01:09:08,680
that would help me keep Trustor.

1241
01:09:08,760 --> 01:09:09,800
But their solution

1242
01:09:09,880 --> 01:09:12,240
was that they would buy Trustor
and take it over.

1243
01:09:12,840 --> 01:09:14,080
No, we didn't meet them.

1244
01:09:15,600 --> 01:09:20,360
There was no meeting
with Joachim and R1 and R2. No.

1245
01:09:21,760 --> 01:09:23,320
I don't think he ever met them.

1246
01:09:25,840 --> 01:09:29,040
Thomas was in a state of panic.
Well, we all were.

1247
01:09:30,080 --> 01:09:31,960
And in that panic,

1248
01:09:32,720 --> 01:09:35,720
he wanted to pass the hot potato to them,

1249
01:09:35,800 --> 01:09:38,600
and cover up that 400 million shortfall.

1250
01:09:38,680 --> 01:09:40,440
I don't recall that.

1251
01:09:41,040 --> 01:09:42,080
Uh…

1252
01:09:42,600 --> 01:09:43,480
No.

1253
01:09:43,560 --> 01:09:46,280
He thought he could
bring a bank statement to Sweden,

1254
01:09:46,360 --> 01:09:49,440
and show them
that the 400 million was still there.

1255
01:09:49,520 --> 01:09:53,240
And that Ricardo and Ricardo
were the new owners.

1256
01:09:53,320 --> 01:09:55,720
But they wanted to pick the company clean.

1257
01:09:55,800 --> 01:09:57,360
I didn't want that.

1258
01:09:57,440 --> 01:10:01,440
Because I realised
that I'd be held accountable for that too.

1259
01:10:01,520 --> 01:10:03,640
So I declined right there and then,

1260
01:10:03,720 --> 01:10:04,960
and we left.

1261
01:10:05,040 --> 01:10:07,960
That was the last time I saw Thomas.

1262
01:10:13,840 --> 01:10:16,600
I was only interested
in owning the company.

1263
01:10:16,680 --> 01:10:21,200
But since the police were involved,
I knew that ship had sailed.

1264
01:10:21,280 --> 01:10:24,440
It was not gonna happen. I left Trustor.

1265
01:10:24,520 --> 01:10:26,400
When I left Geneva,

1266
01:10:26,920 --> 01:10:27,920
I was done.

1267
01:10:31,800 --> 01:10:35,520
I'd split my share of the Trustor deal
across three bank accounts.

1268
01:10:35,600 --> 01:10:37,520
One of them was in Israel.

1269
01:10:38,440 --> 01:10:41,560
I thought my accounts would be frozen
and the funds confiscated.

1270
01:10:42,080 --> 01:10:45,320
I thought I'd withdraw the cash,
hide it, and return home.

1271
01:10:48,120 --> 01:10:50,640
I went to an internet café
and followed the news.

1272
01:10:51,960 --> 01:10:53,560
They hadn't published my picture.

1273
01:10:54,960 --> 01:10:57,840
I called a few trusted friends at home.

1274
01:10:57,920 --> 01:10:59,680
But I didn't contact my family.

1275
01:10:59,760 --> 01:11:02,440
I realised they would be
under police surveillance.

1276
01:11:03,040 --> 01:11:04,720
I was really paranoid.

1277
01:11:07,320 --> 01:11:10,440
[Karin] <i>Since everyone</i>
<i>in Team Moyne was abroad,</i>

1278
01:11:10,520 --> 01:11:12,120
<i>the police had to focus</i>

1279
01:11:12,200 --> 01:11:15,120
<i>on the few people</i>
<i>they could find in Sweden.</i>

1280
01:11:17,440 --> 01:11:21,760
For me, it all clicked into place
over the All Saint's weekend that year.

1281
01:11:22,480 --> 01:11:28,120
My wife and I were driving down to Skåne
with a trailer, carrying random things.

1282
01:11:29,240 --> 01:11:32,280
Bikes and a lawnmower,
things for the summer house.

1283
01:11:32,360 --> 01:11:33,440
[phone ringing]

1284
01:11:33,520 --> 01:11:34,760
Then the phone rang.

1285
01:11:35,280 --> 01:11:39,160
I was a little more irritable than usual.
I answered, "Hello?"

1286
01:11:39,240 --> 01:11:40,480
<i>"Is this Björn Björnsson?"</i>

1287
01:11:40,560 --> 01:11:43,000
"Course it is," I said.
"Who the hell else would it be?"

1288
01:11:43,520 --> 01:11:45,400
<i>"This is the Federal Crime Police."</i>

1289
01:11:45,480 --> 01:11:47,160
I did a U-turn.

1290
01:11:48,280 --> 01:11:50,000
I started driving back and they said…

1291
01:11:50,080 --> 01:11:53,040
<i>"We'd like to hold an interview</i>
<i>with you this evening."</i>

1292
01:11:54,280 --> 01:11:56,480
"Okay," I said,
"I'll be there as fast as I can."

1293
01:11:56,560 --> 01:11:57,760
And then I hung up.

1294
01:11:58,640 --> 01:12:01,800
I drove as fast as I could
from Österlen to Stockholm.

1295
01:12:02,600 --> 01:12:06,000
And when I got there,
I was cross-examined for three hours.

1296
01:12:06,080 --> 01:12:07,640
I was a suspect initially.

1297
01:12:07,720 --> 01:12:09,640
I was furious, to be honest with you.

1298
01:12:10,720 --> 01:12:12,840
This always gives me a hard time.

1299
01:12:13,360 --> 01:12:17,520
[Karin] <i>The police also spoke</i>
<i>to vice president Richard Djursén.</i>

1300
01:12:18,120 --> 01:12:21,880
It was a few hours before I was set to go
on my honeymoon to Mauritius.

1301
01:12:22,760 --> 01:12:24,880
I'd spoken to the police
and everything seemed fine.

1302
01:12:24,960 --> 01:12:26,720
They let me go to Mauritius.

1303
01:12:26,800 --> 01:12:28,240
It was not a fun vacation.

1304
01:12:28,320 --> 01:12:31,960
All the journalists kept calling me.
No one else was picking up the phone.

1305
01:12:32,800 --> 01:12:36,000
[Richard, on phone] <i>I understand</i>
<i>Lindsay Smallbone will be explaining</i>

1306
01:12:36,520 --> 01:12:39,960
{\an8}<i>later today</i>
<i>how the funds have been invested,</i>

1307
01:12:40,040 --> 01:12:42,720
{\an8}<i>what's happened with the money that is…</i>

1308
01:12:43,240 --> 01:12:46,640
{\an8}<i>Or rather,</i>
<i>the money that is not at Barclays Bank.</i>

1309
01:12:47,680 --> 01:12:49,400
[chuckles]

1310
01:12:50,080 --> 01:12:50,960
[groans]

1311
01:12:51,040 --> 01:12:53,520
In hindsight,
it was a disastrous vacation.

1312
01:12:53,600 --> 01:12:57,400
[on phone] <i>I was only ever</i>
<i>the vice president in name only.</i>

1313
01:12:57,480 --> 01:13:00,040
<i>That's just a title that I've been given.</i>

1314
01:13:00,120 --> 01:13:04,280
<i>In the day to day,</i>
<i>I was more of an errand boy, I would say.</i>

1315
01:13:04,800 --> 01:13:07,400
Djursén just couldn't keep his mouth shut.

1316
01:13:07,480 --> 01:13:08,680
He kept yapping.

1317
01:13:08,760 --> 01:13:12,760
{\an8}[Richard, on phone] <i>Had Lindsay Smallbone</i>
<i>and Lord Moyne been a bit more crafty,</i>

1318
01:13:12,840 --> 01:13:16,720
{\an8}<i>they could've easily accessed the account</i>
<i>to rectify things.</i>

1319
01:13:16,800 --> 01:13:18,560
There was no stopping him.

1320
01:13:18,640 --> 01:13:21,040
He kept creating new problems.

1321
01:13:21,120 --> 01:13:24,960
{\an8}[Richard] <i>I've been dragged into something</i>
<i>that has nothing to do with me.</i>

1322
01:13:25,040 --> 01:13:29,240
{\an8}It went so far
that some of my friends called and said,

1323
01:13:29,320 --> 01:13:30,960
{\an8}"Don't talk to journalists."

1324
01:13:31,040 --> 01:13:34,840
{\an8}"It's obvious that you've been drinking
and you're on live TV."

1325
01:13:34,920 --> 01:13:36,920
{\an8}[reporter] <i>So who appointed you?</i>

1326
01:13:38,560 --> 01:13:39,480
{\an8}[Richard] <i>Uh…</i>

1327
01:13:40,280 --> 01:13:43,480
{\an8}<i>Well, officially, I suppose it was…</i>

1328
01:13:45,640 --> 01:13:47,920
{\an8}<i>uh, the board, I think?</i>

1329
01:13:49,280 --> 01:13:50,640
Disaster.

1330
01:13:51,120 --> 01:13:52,440
Still married, so that's good.

1331
01:13:56,760 --> 01:13:58,120
[Joachim] I was in Israel,

1332
01:13:58,200 --> 01:14:00,000
and just watching this story

1333
01:14:00,080 --> 01:14:01,680
{\an8}grow bigger and bigger…

1334
01:14:01,760 --> 01:14:03,120
{\an8}THE BRAINS BEHIND THE COUP?

1335
01:14:03,200 --> 01:14:04,120
{\an8}…and bigger.

1336
01:14:04,200 --> 01:14:05,960
{\an8}HUNTED FOR THE MILLION KRONOR COUP

1337
01:14:06,040 --> 01:14:07,360
{\an8}I was on every front page.

1338
01:14:07,440 --> 01:14:08,600
{\an8}POLICE INVESTIGATE COMPANIES

1339
01:14:09,200 --> 01:14:12,560
The collapse was amazing.

1340
01:14:14,320 --> 01:14:18,360
I mean,
page after page of the British press.

1341
01:14:19,240 --> 01:14:22,880
I mean, everything stopped so quickly.

1342
01:14:24,840 --> 01:14:27,680
One day, it was business.

1343
01:14:27,760 --> 01:14:30,360
The next day, <i>finito.</i>

1344
01:14:32,440 --> 01:14:34,800
[Karin] <i>A week</i>
<i>after the affair came to light,</i>

1345
01:14:34,880 --> 01:14:39,800
<i>Thomas Jisander and Peter Mattsson</i>
<i>left the Riviera and returned to Sweden.</i>

1346
01:14:40,560 --> 01:14:43,480
<i>They had intended to come forward</i>
<i>and face the press,</i>

1347
01:14:43,560 --> 01:14:45,760
<i>but found themselves in custody instead.</i>

1348
01:14:45,840 --> 01:14:47,600
CAME TO FACE THE PRESS,
ENDED UP IN CUSTODY

1349
01:14:48,280 --> 01:14:52,400
I was like, "Man, what's the big deal?
Why don't they just ask their questions?"

1350
01:14:53,000 --> 01:14:55,480
"Let's open a bottle of wine
and talk it out."

1351
01:14:55,560 --> 01:14:57,720
PROSECUTOR DETAINED
BOTH JISANDER AND MATTSSON

1352
01:14:58,320 --> 01:15:00,760
We were there all of 15 minutes at most.

1353
01:15:00,840 --> 01:15:02,640
And that was it, done.

1354
01:15:02,720 --> 01:15:03,760
Detained.

1355
01:15:04,680 --> 01:15:08,000
{\an8}[Karin] <i>Everyone in Team Moyne</i>
<i>was removed from their positions.</i>

1356
01:15:08,080 --> 01:15:09,200
{\an8}FORCED TO RESIGN - DETAINED

1357
01:15:09,280 --> 01:15:11,000
{\an8}<i>Posener was arrested in absentia.</i>

1358
01:15:11,080 --> 01:15:13,320
{\an8}DETAINED IN ABSENTIA

1359
01:15:13,400 --> 01:15:17,200
{\an8}<i>Meanwhile, Björn Björnsson</i>
<i>took on his second role in Trustor.</i>

1360
01:15:17,280 --> 01:15:20,120
{\an8}<i>He was appointed the new CEO</i>
<i>while this was happening.</i>

1361
01:15:21,760 --> 01:15:25,680
It was an extremely messy week
when this all blew up.

1362
01:15:26,240 --> 01:15:27,920
The first thing I did as CEO

1363
01:15:28,000 --> 01:15:31,520
{\an8}was to try and wrap my head around
what actually happened.

1364
01:15:31,600 --> 01:15:32,840
{\an8}NEW CEO, TRUSTOR

1365
01:15:35,400 --> 01:15:38,080
In late fall, early winter,
Björn Björnsson got in touch

1366
01:15:38,160 --> 01:15:40,280
and we met at a lawyer's office.

1367
01:15:41,160 --> 01:15:44,040
I sat there
and told him everything I knew.

1368
01:15:44,120 --> 01:15:46,960
That Team Moyne was intending
to sell some of Trustor's assets

1369
01:15:47,040 --> 01:15:48,320
at far too low a price

1370
01:15:48,400 --> 01:15:51,000
to a previous majority shareholder,
Norberg.

1371
01:15:51,840 --> 01:15:53,320
I prevented that,

1372
01:15:53,400 --> 01:15:55,800
and in doing so
I saved Trustor a lot of money.

1373
01:15:59,560 --> 01:16:00,600
[Björn sighs]

1374
01:16:00,680 --> 01:16:03,800
Well, you can be a useful idiot.

1375
01:16:05,320 --> 01:16:07,520
But that doesn't excuse your actions.

1376
01:16:08,440 --> 01:16:11,800
I saw a vice president
who could not do his job properly.

1377
01:16:12,840 --> 01:16:15,120
It was obvious he'd have to go.

1378
01:16:17,240 --> 01:16:19,520
[Richard] Despite telling them
everything I knew,

1379
01:16:20,040 --> 01:16:21,160
I was fired.

1380
01:16:23,280 --> 01:16:25,080
It was so humiliating.

1381
01:16:28,360 --> 01:16:30,360
That time at Trustor was…

1382
01:16:32,360 --> 01:16:33,680
[snuffles, clicks fingers]

1383
01:16:36,760 --> 01:16:38,080
It's still hard.

1384
01:16:38,760 --> 01:16:40,880
POSENER FALK, JOACHIM RALPH
GROSS BREACH OF TRUST

1385
01:16:40,960 --> 01:16:43,160
[Karin] <i>The last trace of Joachim Posener</i>

1386
01:16:43,240 --> 01:16:45,280
<i>was from November 1997.</i>

1387
01:16:45,360 --> 01:16:46,800
NO KNOWN ADDRESS

1388
01:16:46,880 --> 01:16:48,080
<i>He moved around Europe,</i>

1389
01:16:48,840 --> 01:16:49,920
<i>paid in cash,</i>

1390
01:16:50,000 --> 01:16:52,560
<i>and stayed in hotels using aliases.</i>

1391
01:16:54,080 --> 01:16:56,840
<i>He managed to board a plane</i>
<i>to South America</i>

1392
01:16:56,920 --> 01:17:00,280
{\an8}<i>just days before an international warrant</i>
<i>was issued.</i>

1393
01:17:00,360 --> 01:17:01,560
{\an8}INTERNATIONAL ARREST WARRANT

1394
01:17:01,640 --> 01:17:03,600
[enigmatic music playing]

1395
01:17:11,440 --> 01:17:14,960
[Joachim] I did know somebody
in the Stockholm criminal world,

1396
01:17:15,040 --> 01:17:17,920
and he knew somebody in South America.

1397
01:17:19,240 --> 01:17:23,200
These people are well-organised
and highly dangerous.

1398
01:17:24,320 --> 01:17:29,040
I proceeded to buy what I later learned
is known as a "legend"

1399
01:17:29,120 --> 01:17:30,440
in the world of spies.

1400
01:17:30,520 --> 01:17:33,720
So a shell of a person that you assume.

1401
01:17:33,800 --> 01:17:36,320
They can take decades to create.

1402
01:17:37,200 --> 01:17:38,360
And just like that,

1403
01:17:39,360 --> 01:17:41,000
I was a new man.

1404
01:17:42,440 --> 01:17:47,960
-[driver] Is it the next one?
-[Joachim] Yes, straight, and then right.

1405
01:17:49,120 --> 01:17:52,080
I became another person,
who already existed.

1406
01:17:52,160 --> 01:17:56,200
-[woman] Look at his face. So swollen.
-[man] Actually, it's gone down a bit.

1407
01:17:57,920 --> 01:18:01,440
[Joachim] These people hid me
in a small village in Brazil.

1408
01:18:02,840 --> 01:18:06,360
I lived there for many years.

1409
01:18:06,440 --> 01:18:08,840
-Hello!
-Hello!

1410
01:18:11,040 --> 01:18:15,440
[Joachim] I spent a lot of time
in a favela, the local slum.

1411
01:18:18,400 --> 01:18:19,960
The police never went there.

1412
01:18:20,560 --> 01:18:22,760
You don't go there uninvited.

1413
01:18:22,840 --> 01:18:25,560
-[indistinct, lively chatter]
-[guitar strumming]

1414
01:18:26,400 --> 01:18:29,480
[Joachim] The territory
was controlled by a drug cartel,

1415
01:18:29,560 --> 01:18:32,120
and they had soldiers at every entrance.

1416
01:18:33,160 --> 01:18:34,880
Nobody would find me there.

1417
01:18:35,400 --> 01:18:37,880
[ominous music playing]

1418
01:18:37,960 --> 01:18:39,960
[news theme playing]

1419
01:18:43,680 --> 01:18:47,640
{\an8}Good evening.
Recent developments in the Trustor saga…

1420
01:18:48,560 --> 01:18:50,800
{\an8}[Karin] <i>During the fall of 1997,</i>

1421
01:18:50,880 --> 01:18:54,680
{\an8}<i>news anchors in colourful ties</i>
<i>continued to report on the Trustor saga.</i>

1422
01:18:54,760 --> 01:18:55,640
…looting of funds.

1423
01:18:55,720 --> 01:18:59,120
The looting of Trustor assets
worth hundreds of millions.

1424
01:18:59,200 --> 01:19:01,360
[Karin] <i>Everybody talked of "looting."</i>

1425
01:19:01,440 --> 01:19:05,320
The looting of Trustor's assets
might never be resolved.

1426
01:19:05,400 --> 01:19:06,600
THE MOST BRAZEN LOOTING

1427
01:19:06,680 --> 01:19:09,120
[Karin] <i>One question remained unanswered,</i>

1428
01:19:09,200 --> 01:19:11,400
<i>where is the money from Trustor?</i>

1429
01:19:11,480 --> 01:19:14,360
OH MY LORD, WHERE'S THE MONEY?

1430
01:19:18,600 --> 01:19:21,080
[Joachim] Around 400 million was missing.

1431
01:19:22,280 --> 01:19:26,520
I had used 240 million
to pay the former owner, Norberg.

1432
01:19:28,080 --> 01:19:31,880
The money had been converted into shares
and pledged to the bank.

1433
01:19:31,960 --> 01:19:34,200
So when the police
were looking for the money,

1434
01:19:34,280 --> 01:19:36,040
it's there, as shares.

1435
01:19:38,840 --> 01:19:43,240
There had been speculation about
how much I'd made from the Trustor deal.

1436
01:19:43,960 --> 01:19:47,000
I paid myself ten million in total.

1437
01:19:47,080 --> 01:19:48,960
That's the true figure.

1438
01:19:50,720 --> 01:19:53,520
Maybe not what you were expecting,
but it's true.

1439
01:19:55,560 --> 01:19:58,520
I was planning
to take out ten million a year in salary.

1440
01:19:58,600 --> 01:20:01,360
That was the plan
for the long-term, anyway.

1441
01:20:01,880 --> 01:20:04,520
But nothing turned out
as I had planned, of course,

1442
01:20:04,600 --> 01:20:07,840
and half of the ten million
was frozen by the police and Trustor,

1443
01:20:07,920 --> 01:20:10,800
so I never even got
the full amount of that.

1444
01:20:12,160 --> 01:20:13,960
And then we have Thomas's fee.

1445
01:20:14,040 --> 01:20:16,880
He got five million,
but wasn't satisfied with that.

1446
01:20:16,960 --> 01:20:19,520
From what I understand,
he took another 90 million.

1447
01:20:20,240 --> 01:20:23,160
But that happened behind my back.
It didn't go through me.

1448
01:20:25,160 --> 01:20:28,000
What mattered to me
was paying back the 20 million

1449
01:20:28,080 --> 01:20:30,160
I owed to the Swedish gangsters.

1450
01:20:30,240 --> 01:20:34,440
That way, I wouldn't be in their debt
and wouldn't have problems in the future.

1451
01:20:37,240 --> 01:20:40,120
And 70 million went to various expenses.

1452
01:20:40,720 --> 01:20:43,920
Salaries, travel expenses, office rentals.

1453
01:20:44,000 --> 01:20:46,960
Compensation to Lord Moyne,
Lindsay and Peter.

1454
01:20:47,480 --> 01:20:50,400
I bought Trustor,
but I didn't loot the company.

1455
01:20:51,360 --> 01:20:54,680
[Karin] You looted company assets
by buying it with its own money,

1456
01:20:54,760 --> 01:20:58,000
and using the accounts for furnishings,
travel expenses, vacations…

1457
01:20:58,080 --> 01:21:00,320
[Joachim] But if I write,

1458
01:21:01,080 --> 01:21:02,160
uh,

1459
01:21:02,240 --> 01:21:04,160
an invoice, that's not looting.

1460
01:21:04,240 --> 01:21:05,480
It's a business expense.

1461
01:21:05,560 --> 01:21:08,320
I bought a company. I didn't rob anyone.

1462
01:21:08,840 --> 01:21:11,560
[Karin] So if it's not stealing,
then what is it?

1463
01:21:12,080 --> 01:21:15,360
I bought the company
using an unauthorised loan.

1464
01:21:16,920 --> 01:21:17,960
That's it.

1465
01:21:28,080 --> 01:21:30,840
[Joachim] This is where we live.
We're in the kitchen.

1466
01:21:30,920 --> 01:21:31,880
[clears throat]

1467
01:21:36,640 --> 01:21:38,280
I'm boiling some water

1468
01:21:39,200 --> 01:21:40,680
for breakfast.

1469
01:21:41,480 --> 01:21:44,720
I'm sorry,
I couldn't be bothered to clean.

1470
01:21:45,840 --> 01:21:47,560
The dishwasher can't handle it all.

1471
01:21:47,640 --> 01:21:49,200
We went out to buy some bread.

1472
01:21:49,720 --> 01:21:52,760
I lived off the money from Trustor
for about three years.

1473
01:21:56,160 --> 01:21:58,760
Life on the run is very expensive.

1474
01:21:58,840 --> 01:22:01,360
So is buying a new identity

1475
01:22:01,440 --> 01:22:03,600
and not being able to work.

1476
01:22:04,280 --> 01:22:05,920
It's expensive

1477
01:22:06,560 --> 01:22:08,840
pretending to be somebody else.

1478
01:22:09,560 --> 01:22:11,680
I've seen a lot of this view.

1479
01:22:14,240 --> 01:22:15,720
In order to avoid being found,

1480
01:22:15,800 --> 01:22:18,680
you need to look completely different
to what people expect.

1481
01:22:19,800 --> 01:22:23,400
So curly, black-haired Joachim
shaved his head.

1482
01:22:23,480 --> 01:22:26,800
Chubby Joachim became fit Joachim.

1483
01:22:27,560 --> 01:22:29,520
I swapped glasses for contacts.

1484
01:22:29,600 --> 01:22:31,520
I obviously never went home.

1485
01:22:31,600 --> 01:22:33,240
That would have been idiotic.

1486
01:22:33,320 --> 01:22:34,880
First, I stayed in Brazil.

1487
01:22:34,960 --> 01:22:39,240
When the media found out about Brazil,
I'd already moved back to Europe.

1488
01:22:44,560 --> 01:22:46,080
While Joachim was on the run,

1489
01:22:46,160 --> 01:22:48,200
there were all these media reports

1490
01:22:48,280 --> 01:22:51,800
that he'd been spotted
somewhere or another.

1491
01:22:53,240 --> 01:22:57,160
Police believe that a picture
taken by a tourist in South Africa

1492
01:22:57,240 --> 01:22:59,680
is the wanted Joachim Posener.

1493
01:23:00,920 --> 01:23:02,800
[Thomas] They published this picture.

1494
01:23:02,880 --> 01:23:06,280
Those of us who knew him said right away,
"Jesus Christ, that's not him."

1495
01:23:06,800 --> 01:23:09,600
If true, the seven-year manhunt
may have some life again.

1496
01:23:10,560 --> 01:23:12,360
"Have we finally found him?"

1497
01:23:12,440 --> 01:23:14,760
"Is this the end of the manhunt?"

1498
01:23:15,840 --> 01:23:19,000
HOW POSENER'S FOOLING THE POLICE

1499
01:23:19,080 --> 01:23:22,320
Various facial composites were created.
Oh, my God.

1500
01:23:22,400 --> 01:23:25,400
There were probably 50 people
who those could have been.

1501
01:23:25,480 --> 01:23:27,480
[curious music playing]

1502
01:23:28,400 --> 01:23:29,640
[music ends]

1503
01:23:31,400 --> 01:23:33,120
[objects clattering]

1504
01:23:37,240 --> 01:23:39,200
[Richard] Hold on, where did I put it?

1505
01:23:39,880 --> 01:23:41,840
-Is this it?
-[clattering continues]

1506
01:23:42,640 --> 01:23:43,880
Okay, here it is.

1507
01:23:44,400 --> 01:23:45,520
There's a lot in here.

1508
01:23:46,040 --> 01:23:46,960
Check this out.

1509
01:23:47,040 --> 01:23:48,520
Newspaper clippings.

1510
01:23:48,600 --> 01:23:50,480
There's a ton of them.

1511
01:23:59,600 --> 01:24:02,320
They used
the worst picture they could find.

1512
01:24:03,360 --> 01:24:05,200
I found that insulting, actually.

1513
01:24:05,720 --> 01:24:07,280
[tuts, laughs]

1514
01:24:08,040 --> 01:24:09,320
This is a nicer picture.

1515
01:24:09,920 --> 01:24:11,520
It doesn't embarrass me.

1516
01:24:12,040 --> 01:24:13,360
Such bullshit.

1517
01:24:17,960 --> 01:24:19,680
[Richard sighs]

1518
01:24:20,360 --> 01:24:22,080
Six months after the Trustor scandal,

1519
01:24:22,160 --> 01:24:24,920
I had a one-year-old son
and newborn twins.

1520
01:24:28,280 --> 01:24:30,800
I had no job, all my accounts were frozen,

1521
01:24:30,880 --> 01:24:33,640
and nobody would touch me
with a ten-foot pole.

1522
01:24:35,200 --> 01:24:37,320
I had to sell the house.

1523
01:24:38,400 --> 01:24:41,560
And we moved
to a small rental apartment in Hägersten.

1524
01:24:42,440 --> 01:24:44,600
My life changed completely.

1525
01:24:46,800 --> 01:24:49,560
I lost everything, except my family.

1526
01:24:50,120 --> 01:24:53,600
I wanted to take revenge
on all those people who'd hurt me.

1527
01:24:53,680 --> 01:24:56,560
And the person I was most angry with
was Björn Björnsson,

1528
01:24:56,640 --> 01:24:58,640
because he threw me under the bus.

1529
01:25:03,040 --> 01:25:05,600
Because of that, I wanted to end him.

1530
01:25:06,240 --> 01:25:09,720
I drove around where he lives
in Djursholm, past his house.

1531
01:25:09,800 --> 01:25:11,640
He doesn't know about this.

1532
01:25:13,360 --> 01:25:17,520
So I was driving around there
in my car, and…

1533
01:25:18,640 --> 01:25:20,000
This is so crazy.

1534
01:25:21,480 --> 01:25:23,800
At one point I could've written a book

1535
01:25:23,880 --> 01:25:26,880
on 300 different ways of killing somebody

1536
01:25:26,960 --> 01:25:28,200
without getting caught.

1537
01:25:28,720 --> 01:25:32,240
Everything from buying a wood chipper
and putting the corpse in,

1538
01:25:32,320 --> 01:25:35,600
then spreading the remains at sea
for the fish to eat.

1539
01:25:36,120 --> 01:25:40,200
You need to dispose of the body somehow.

1540
01:25:40,280 --> 01:25:43,640
There was no Google at the time,
but you could still find out

1541
01:25:44,320 --> 01:25:46,200
how to cremate stuff.

1542
01:25:46,280 --> 01:25:48,160
It's done with high heat, of course.

1543
01:25:48,240 --> 01:25:49,960
You can build it yourself.

1544
01:25:50,040 --> 01:25:53,800
I was going to rent a cabin
in northern Sweden

1545
01:25:53,880 --> 01:25:56,000
and build one of those cremation furnaces

1546
01:25:57,680 --> 01:26:00,120
where all traces are destroyed.

1547
01:26:04,360 --> 01:26:06,960
I sat here
watching Björn Björnsson's house.

1548
01:26:07,840 --> 01:26:08,960
I drove around

1549
01:26:09,040 --> 01:26:12,240
checking different escape routes
in his area

1550
01:26:13,000 --> 01:26:15,800
that would allow me to get away quickly.

1551
01:26:16,560 --> 01:26:18,720
I thought I needed to turn myself in.

1552
01:26:18,800 --> 01:26:20,960
I called psychiatric services in Nacka.

1553
01:26:21,600 --> 01:26:24,880
I told them
that I thought I needed to be committed,

1554
01:26:24,960 --> 01:26:28,840
since I was considering… killing someone.

1555
01:26:29,360 --> 01:26:33,040
You only have such violent thoughts
when you're depressed.

1556
01:26:33,680 --> 01:26:35,880
[Karin] Do you still have those thoughts?

1557
01:26:35,960 --> 01:26:38,040
[Richard] Not at all. They're long gone.

1558
01:26:40,960 --> 01:26:42,960
Shit, I didn't start crying. That's weird.

1559
01:26:43,480 --> 01:26:44,560
[chuckles]

1560
01:26:45,920 --> 01:26:46,840
Oh, dear.

1561
01:26:51,160 --> 01:26:53,400
I thought I'd be crying the whole time.

1562
01:26:54,640 --> 01:26:55,480
No.

1563
01:26:58,680 --> 01:27:02,800
As long as… I'm talking
and keep going, it's fine.

1564
01:27:03,320 --> 01:27:04,720
I can keep from crying.

1565
01:27:06,280 --> 01:27:07,400
But actually…

1566
01:27:07,920 --> 01:27:08,880
[hesitates, coughs]

1567
01:27:08,960 --> 01:27:10,080
No, forget it.

1568
01:27:15,440 --> 01:27:17,000
[breathes deeply]

1569
01:27:17,080 --> 01:27:19,120
[cries quietly]

1570
01:27:21,200 --> 01:27:22,120
Hm.

1571
01:27:24,120 --> 01:27:25,720
[Richard sniffling on video]

1572
01:27:26,680 --> 01:27:28,880
It's tragic to see how he's ended up.

1573
01:27:30,600 --> 01:27:32,560
Even considering where he's from.

1574
01:27:35,000 --> 01:27:36,000
[Richard sighs]

1575
01:27:38,120 --> 01:27:39,760
But he seems to be doing alright.

1576
01:27:39,840 --> 01:27:42,000
He's driving a Porsche
and has a nice house.

1577
01:27:42,080 --> 01:27:44,040
He's doing well financially.

1578
01:27:44,600 --> 01:27:46,080
[dramatic music playing]

1579
01:27:46,160 --> 01:27:49,080
STOCKHOLM DISTRICT COURT
2001

1580
01:27:49,160 --> 01:27:52,760
<i>Today saw the start of the trial</i>
<i>of those involved in the looting of assets</i>

1581
01:27:52,840 --> 01:27:54,120
<i>from Trustor.</i>

1582
01:27:56,600 --> 01:27:58,520
[Karin] <i>Financial crime is hard to prove,</i>

1583
01:27:58,600 --> 01:28:01,640
<i>and becomes even more complicated</i>
<i>when committed abroad.</i>

1584
01:28:02,600 --> 01:28:05,360
<i>In this case,</i>
<i>the key figure was also missing,</i>

1585
01:28:05,440 --> 01:28:09,000
<i>which meant that the legal proceedings</i>
<i>were doomed to fail.</i>

1586
01:28:10,640 --> 01:28:13,720
<i>Lindsay Smallbone was not prosecuted</i>
<i>and walked free.</i>

1587
01:28:13,800 --> 01:28:16,880
<i>New Zealand</i>
<i>has no extradition agreement with Sweden.</i>

1588
01:28:16,960 --> 01:28:18,840
<i>Lord Moyne was prosecuted,</i>

1589
01:28:19,360 --> 01:28:24,160
<i>but claimed that some of the signatures</i>
<i>on the Trustor documents were not his.</i>

1590
01:28:24,680 --> 01:28:26,000
<i>He also walked free.</i>

1591
01:28:26,080 --> 01:28:27,040
FRONTMAN WALKS FREE

1592
01:28:27,640 --> 01:28:30,960
-[man] Why were you important for them?
-Name.

1593
01:28:31,480 --> 01:28:32,720
The name.

1594
01:28:34,080 --> 01:28:35,200
I'm bankrupt.

1595
01:28:35,720 --> 01:28:37,600
It's as simple as that.

1596
01:28:39,400 --> 01:28:41,800
[Karin] <i>Peter Mattsson and Thomas Jisander</i>

1597
01:28:41,880 --> 01:28:44,640
<i>were initially convicted</i>
<i>by the district court.</i>

1598
01:28:44,720 --> 01:28:46,640
[Thomas] I was sentenced
to five years in prison,

1599
01:28:46,720 --> 01:28:48,320
a nine-year ban on business activity

1600
01:28:48,400 --> 01:28:50,680
and had to pay 100 million in damages.

1601
01:28:51,800 --> 01:28:54,560
[Karin] <i>But they appealed the decision.</i>

1602
01:28:55,600 --> 01:28:57,960
This time round, we were better prepared.

1603
01:28:58,480 --> 01:29:00,920
FRESH START IN TRUSTOR CASE

1604
01:29:02,400 --> 01:29:04,480
[Karin] <i>Since the key figure was missing,</i>

1605
01:29:04,560 --> 01:29:06,560
<i>it became convenient to blame him.</i>

1606
01:29:06,640 --> 01:29:07,600
{\an8}"TRICKED BY POSENER"

1607
01:29:07,680 --> 01:29:09,080
{\an8}[Joachim] During the trial,

1608
01:29:09,160 --> 01:29:12,880
{\an8}they came up with absurd arguments
for their innocence.

1609
01:29:12,960 --> 01:29:14,160
{\an8}THE PROSECUTED BLAME POSENER

1610
01:29:14,240 --> 01:29:17,080
{\an8}The prosecutor claimed to have found
incriminating documents

1611
01:29:17,160 --> 01:29:19,880
on the computer found in my apartment.

1612
01:29:20,400 --> 01:29:21,720
But who used that computer?

1613
01:29:22,800 --> 01:29:24,880
We brought in a technical expert

1614
01:29:24,960 --> 01:29:26,640
who demonstrated to the court

1615
01:29:26,720 --> 01:29:29,800
{\an8}how easy it would be
to access a computer remotely.

1616
01:29:29,880 --> 01:29:31,880
We were able to prove
that was a possibility.

1617
01:29:31,960 --> 01:29:33,040
PROGRAM FOR DATA TRANSFER

1618
01:29:33,120 --> 01:29:37,760
Then it was in the hands of the court,
and evidently they believed it, as well.

1619
01:29:39,080 --> 01:29:41,720
{\an8}Today they were acquitted
by the court of appeal.

1620
01:29:41,800 --> 01:29:43,760
There was not enough evidence

1621
01:29:43,840 --> 01:29:46,840
against Thomas Jisander
and Peter Mattsson.

1622
01:29:47,360 --> 01:29:48,760
{\an8}It's been incredibly tough,

1623
01:29:48,840 --> 01:29:52,960
{\an8}but it's with great relief I can say that,
luckily, there is justice in this world.

1624
01:29:53,040 --> 01:30:00,040
TRUSTOR SCANDAL VILLAINS WALK FREE

1625
01:30:07,240 --> 01:30:09,280
[Jochum] Posener was never convicted.

1626
01:30:09,360 --> 01:30:10,400
He vanished.

1627
01:30:11,800 --> 01:30:13,520
And we've not heard from, or seen…

1628
01:30:13,600 --> 01:30:14,720
[golfer] Fore!

1629
01:30:14,800 --> 01:30:15,840
Sorry.

1630
01:30:16,440 --> 01:30:19,200
He's gone up in smoke, so to speak.

1631
01:30:22,080 --> 01:30:23,400
I left the police force.

1632
01:30:23,480 --> 01:30:25,680
I needed to try something different.

1633
01:30:26,400 --> 01:30:28,240
I started working at a golf club.

1634
01:30:31,440 --> 01:30:35,360
It obviously haunts me
that we never caught Joachim Posener.

1635
01:30:36,320 --> 01:30:37,160
What the…

1636
01:30:37,680 --> 01:30:41,040
It would give closure,
an ending to it all.

1637
01:30:42,680 --> 01:30:43,840
That's how I feel.

1638
01:30:46,200 --> 01:30:50,160
I find it strange
that you can stay away for 30 years.

1639
01:30:51,160 --> 01:30:52,640
Not seeing your family,

1640
01:30:52,720 --> 01:30:55,080
and having to look over your shoulder.

1641
01:30:56,000 --> 01:30:58,560
It must be like losing your identity.

1642
01:31:01,400 --> 01:31:03,400
[lively chatter in background]

1643
01:31:07,160 --> 01:31:10,040
[Joachim] Being in hiding
means I've been able to live a life

1644
01:31:10,120 --> 01:31:11,520
on my own terms.

1645
01:31:13,200 --> 01:31:15,960
Where I live, nobody calls me Joachim…

1646
01:31:17,040 --> 01:31:19,240
Charlie, how are you, my friend?

1647
01:31:19,320 --> 01:31:21,200
How are you? Good to see you.

1648
01:31:21,280 --> 01:31:22,360
See you soon.

1649
01:31:24,600 --> 01:31:27,080
…despite the fact
that I regained my passport

1650
01:31:27,160 --> 01:31:29,720
and my real name a long time ago.

1651
01:31:39,320 --> 01:31:41,000
[Karin] What's your life like?

1652
01:31:42,200 --> 01:31:44,640
[Joachim] I live kind of

1653
01:31:45,320 --> 01:31:47,520
a bohemian lifestyle.

1654
01:31:48,880 --> 01:31:49,760
There.

1655
01:31:49,840 --> 01:31:52,680
Not in my native country,

1656
01:31:52,760 --> 01:31:55,520
not even in my wife's native country.

1657
01:31:56,640 --> 01:31:59,960
One foot in society and one outside.

1658
01:32:02,520 --> 01:32:05,200
Do I need to make a living? Absolutely.

1659
01:32:05,840 --> 01:32:07,800
I've worked with what I know best,

1660
01:32:07,880 --> 01:32:10,160
as a consultant and advisor.

1661
01:32:10,680 --> 01:32:12,480
But in the shadows.

1662
01:32:20,600 --> 01:32:23,240
[woman] What do you want
people to know about you?

1663
01:32:24,640 --> 01:32:26,280
[Joachim] It was never about money.

1664
01:32:26,360 --> 01:32:29,120
It was about… the challenge.

1665
01:32:29,200 --> 01:32:32,840
The adrenaline you get from such deals
is my drug.

1666
01:32:33,360 --> 01:32:36,440
Yeah, it can be hard to stop
once you've started.

1667
01:32:38,240 --> 01:32:39,400
Have you got a family?

1668
01:32:39,480 --> 01:32:42,200
Yes. A wife and two kids.

1669
01:32:42,280 --> 01:32:44,120
-[woman] Girls or boys?
-Girls.

1670
01:32:44,200 --> 01:32:45,920
Do you get to see them?

1671
01:32:46,000 --> 01:32:48,520
-I live with my youngest.
-Okay.

1672
01:32:48,600 --> 01:32:52,160
And I've promised
not to talk about my other daughter.

1673
01:32:52,960 --> 01:32:54,120
How old are they?

1674
01:32:55,600 --> 01:32:59,120
The youngest is 15
and the older one is 32.

1675
01:32:59,720 --> 01:33:00,920
[woman] The same age as me.

1676
01:33:01,520 --> 01:33:03,040
Then I could be your daughter.

1677
01:33:03,560 --> 01:33:05,000
Yes, actually.

1678
01:33:12,400 --> 01:33:15,400
[Karin] The biggest victim
might be your daughter.

1679
01:33:15,920 --> 01:33:17,040
What are your thoughts?

1680
01:33:18,080 --> 01:33:20,800
It is extremely sad and tragic.

1681
01:33:21,920 --> 01:33:24,280
But I wouldn't have…

1682
01:33:24,840 --> 01:33:28,000
I would have gone insane
spending ten more years in prison.

1683
01:33:29,120 --> 01:33:30,520
I couldn't do it.

1684
01:33:31,640 --> 01:33:33,440
[Karin] Given how things turned out…

1685
01:33:33,520 --> 01:33:37,240
You've lived in hiding and lost contact
with your family and your daughter.

1686
01:33:37,760 --> 01:33:39,000
Was it worth it?

1687
01:33:40,640 --> 01:33:42,280
That's a very complicated…

1688
01:33:42,360 --> 01:33:44,960
A simple,
yet complicated question, because…

1689
01:33:45,880 --> 01:33:48,240
Had I not done the Trustor deal,

1690
01:33:49,080 --> 01:33:51,880
I would not have my current wife,

1691
01:33:51,960 --> 01:33:53,440
or my child.

1692
01:33:53,520 --> 01:33:56,880
Was it worth
not spending another ten years in prison?

1693
01:33:56,960 --> 01:33:58,640
Absolutely.

1694
01:33:59,720 --> 01:34:03,720
[Karin] And what about the price
that your family in Sweden had to pay?

1695
01:34:04,240 --> 01:34:06,440
It was worth it for me,
but maybe not for them.

1696
01:34:08,080 --> 01:34:10,600
[tense, pulsating music playing]

1697
01:34:13,400 --> 01:34:17,000
[Karin] <i>On to the most absurd consequence</i>
<i>of the whole affair,</i>

1698
01:34:18,000 --> 01:34:21,960
<i>Trustor's shareholders profited big time.</i>

1699
01:34:23,400 --> 01:34:25,280
<i>In order to understand this,</i>

1700
01:34:25,360 --> 01:34:28,960
<i>we need to look at Björn Björnsson's</i>
<i>third and last role,</i>

1701
01:34:29,040 --> 01:34:32,720
<i>as the liquidator</i>
<i>tasked with winding down Trustor.</i>

1702
01:34:33,240 --> 01:34:36,680
Our mission was to recover
as much money as possible.

1703
01:34:37,200 --> 01:34:39,560
Pay off all the debts,
sell all the assets.

1704
01:34:39,640 --> 01:34:42,720
Whatever was left
went to the shareholders as dividends.

1705
01:34:43,680 --> 01:34:45,120
150 MIL INVESTED AT
STOCK EXCHANGE

1706
01:34:45,200 --> 01:34:49,360
[Karin] <i>The liquidators found money</i>
<i>in Team Moyne's accounts around the world.</i>

1707
01:34:49,440 --> 01:34:50,360
770 MIL
BARCLAYS BANK

1708
01:34:51,080 --> 01:34:55,680
<i>Thomas Jisander was ordered</i>
<i>to pay back 65 million in a settlement.</i>

1709
01:34:56,200 --> 01:34:57,320
{\an8}BARCLAYS BANK SUED

1710
01:34:57,400 --> 01:35:00,880
{\an8}<i>The banks involved</i>
<i>were sued for substantial amounts,</i>

1711
01:35:01,720 --> 01:35:05,080
<i>and Trustor's undervalued assets</i>
<i>were sold.</i>

1712
01:35:07,280 --> 01:35:09,920
<i>So despite the missing money,</i>

1713
01:35:10,000 --> 01:35:14,040
<i>the value of the shares doubled</i>
<i>after the scandal.</i>

1714
01:35:14,120 --> 01:35:16,080
THE TRUSTOR
SCANDAL IS REVEALED

1715
01:35:16,920 --> 01:35:17,920
[Björn sighs]

1716
01:35:19,480 --> 01:35:22,680
It's ironic
that the shareholders got a good deal.

1717
01:35:27,320 --> 01:35:31,200
[Karin] <i>Crimes had been committed,</i>
<i>but the establishment lost out.</i>

1718
01:35:32,160 --> 01:35:36,320
<i>The taxpayers paid the bill</i>
<i>for work carried out by the authorities.</i>

1719
01:35:36,400 --> 01:35:38,520
<i>And everyone involved walked free.</i>

1720
01:35:39,040 --> 01:35:41,120
<i>Well, nearly everyone.</i>

1721
01:35:42,760 --> 01:35:43,960
<i>As some say,</i>

1722
01:35:44,040 --> 01:35:45,280
<i>why follow the law</i>

1723
01:35:45,360 --> 01:35:48,000
<i>when you can treat it as a guideline?</i>

1724
01:35:48,920 --> 01:35:50,920
[wistful music playing]

1725
01:35:53,080 --> 01:35:54,880
[Richard] I'm doing great now.

1726
01:35:56,560 --> 01:35:57,560
Just dandy.

1727
01:35:58,360 --> 01:35:59,760
I've got a good life.

1728
01:36:00,360 --> 01:36:02,400
I've worked hard.

1729
01:36:04,080 --> 01:36:06,440
I've started businesses
that have done really well.

1730
01:36:06,520 --> 01:36:09,000
I've sold businesses and made a fortune.

1731
01:36:12,080 --> 01:36:16,600
I am now financially independent
and can do whatever I want.

1732
01:36:20,960 --> 01:36:23,360
[wistful music continues]

1733
01:36:25,520 --> 01:36:28,320
[Thomas] Well, as I said,
"Nobody remembers a coward."

1734
01:36:29,880 --> 01:36:34,880
Every krona that came out of Trustor,
in one way or another, has been spent.

1735
01:36:36,320 --> 01:36:38,400
It was completely impossible to predict

1736
01:36:38,480 --> 01:36:41,840
that I would earn as little
from this transaction as I did.

1737
01:36:44,080 --> 01:36:46,080
[laughs quietly]

1738
01:36:55,480 --> 01:36:59,480
[Joachim] After Trustor,
I knew I had made my mark on the world.

1739
01:37:01,840 --> 01:37:03,800
That was satisfying.

1740
01:37:05,080 --> 01:37:08,840
But what drove me to it
is no longer in me.

1741
01:37:09,520 --> 01:37:11,680
The freedom I sought through money

1742
01:37:11,760 --> 01:37:14,640
has been replaced
with another kind of freedom.

1743
01:37:15,160 --> 01:37:17,360
One where no one can control me.

1744
01:37:17,880 --> 01:37:20,320
And I choose where I want to be.

1745
01:37:22,400 --> 01:37:24,680
And also choose when I vanish.

1746
01:37:28,600 --> 01:37:29,800
[Thomas whistles]

1747
01:37:30,440 --> 01:37:33,320
[Joachim] The crazy thing
is that Thomas got in touch with me

1748
01:37:33,400 --> 01:37:34,720
during the trial.

1749
01:37:36,840 --> 01:37:38,160
And he asked me,

1750
01:37:39,040 --> 01:37:40,600
"Can we do it again?"

1751
01:37:41,520 --> 01:37:43,920
[suspenseful music playing]

1752
01:37:48,800 --> 01:37:51,160
THOMAS JISANDER WAS SENTENCED
YEARS LATER

1753
01:37:51,240 --> 01:37:52,560
TO A SHORT PRISON TERM

1754
01:37:52,640 --> 01:37:54,760
FOR INCITEMENT TO GROSS EMBEZZLEMENT

1755
01:37:56,160 --> 01:37:57,920
"IT WAS A WONDERFUL

1756
01:37:58,000 --> 01:38:00,080
SIX-MONTH SPA EXPERIENCE!"

1757
01:38:00,160 --> 01:38:01,560
THOMAS JISANDER

1758
01:38:02,760 --> 01:38:04,320
LORD MOYNE'S FAMILY INFORMED US

1759
01:38:04,400 --> 01:38:06,680
THAT HE CAN'T TAKE PART
DUE TO HEALTH REASONS

1760
01:38:06,760 --> 01:38:09,120
PETER MATTSSON, HOWEVER, HASN'T REPLIED

1761
01:38:10,080 --> 01:38:13,000
LINDSAY SMALLBONE HAS PASSED AWAY

1762
01:38:14,040 --> 01:38:17,840
NAPOLEON'S DESK HAS NOT BEEN FOUND

1763
01:38:20,240 --> 01:38:22,640
[energetic synth pop music playing]

1764
01:38:22,720 --> 01:38:25,720
A FILM BY
KARIN AF KLINTBERG

1765
01:39:08,840 --> 01:39:10,840
[dog barking inside]

1766
01:39:23,160 --> 01:39:25,160
[muffled chatter]

1767
01:39:27,200 --> 01:39:29,120
{\an8}[synth pop music continues]

1768
01:40:46,920 --> 01:40:49,440
Just have a look at my fire.

1769
01:40:49,960 --> 01:40:50,800
[short beep]

1770
01:40:50,880 --> 01:40:52,440
Magical fire.

1771
01:40:52,520 --> 01:40:55,880
Several people have looked and said,
"Oh, what a lovely fire."

1772
01:40:56,400 --> 01:40:57,960
Thinking it's a real fire.

1773
01:40:58,040 --> 01:41:00,440
[clock ticking]